-- Delaware General Corporation Law (8 Del. C. ch. 1), sections 204-205 and 211-220 -- THE SEAT LAYER for piece dg4.
--
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock in a Delaware corporation under the General Corporation Law: an
-- incorporator, a director or officer, a stockholder including a minority stockholder. They ask what the Law lets them do,
-- what it requires of them, what they may require of the corporation, and what can be done to them. The Secretary of State,
-- the Court of Chancery and the Attorney General get no seat: what the Court may do appears as what the person may ask it
-- for and what the corporation, directors and stockholders are liable to.
--
-- Nothing here is new law. Every question calls rules of the layer-1 modules imported above and restates none of them.
-- PLAIN INPUTS: each question takes one input per fact the person can state (yes/no, a number, a date, or a choice from a
-- list), each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked. Where a layer-1 rule takes a record, a MAYBE or a list of
-- records, the record is built inside the question, in its WHERE, from those answers; a MAYBE becomes a yes/no and a value,
-- and the value is ignored when the answer is "no". A record field that the rule called never reads is given a fixed
-- placeholder, with a comment saying so.
--
-- WHERE A QUESTION CAN COME BACK EMPTY. A question that returns MAYBE returns NOTHING (not covered) where the text does not
-- answer it; for the questions that ask what ss 211 to 214 and 216 say, NOTHING also means that s 215(a) takes that provision
-- out of a nonstock corporation (the member's questions are in the group for s 215).
--
-- Judgments the Law hands to someone else are facts the person states, never guessed: whether the purpose is "reasonably
-- related to a stockholder's interest as a stockholder" (s 220(a)(2)), whether an interest is "sufficient in law" to support an
-- irrevocable proxy (s 212(e)), whether the board's notice was "prompt" (s 204(g)), and what the Court of Chancery has ordered or
-- determined. The questions assume the text of the Law as of the enactments through 85 Del. Laws, c. 550 (the date in the
-- source file); the Law states no commencement rule in this range (NOTES.md).

-- Situation: a corporate act or an issue of stock may be void or voidable for a failure of authorization (a "defective corporate act"),
-- so that the board is ratifying it or someone is asking the Court of Chancery about it. A form can ask "Has this happened to you?" first.
§ `s 204 and s 205: a defective corporate act, its ratification, and the Court of Chancery`

§§ `s 204(h) What is a defective corporate act, and what is my stock?`

-- src:714 | (h) As used in this section and in § 205 of this title only, the term:
-- src:715 | (1) “Defective corporate act” means an overissue, an election or appointment of directors that is void or voidable due to a failure of authorization, or any act or transaction purportedly taken by or on behalf of the corporation that is, and at the time such act or transaction was purportedly taken would have been, within the power of a corporation under subchapter II of this chapter (without regard to the failure of authorization identified in § 204(b)(1)(D) of this title), but is void or voidable due to a failure of authorization;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(h)(1) (src:714-715)
@export Is the act a defective corporate act (s 204(h)(1))?
GIVEN `the act is an overissue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act an overissue of shares (more shares than the corporation had the power to issue, or shares of a class or series not authorized)?
      `the act is an election or appointment of directors that is void or voidable due to a failure of authorization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an election or appointment of directors that is void or voidable because it was not properly authorized?
      `the act or transaction was purportedly taken by or on behalf of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it an act or transaction purportedly taken by or on behalf of the corporation?
      `the act or transaction is, and when purportedly taken would have been, within the power of a corporation under subchapter II, ignoring the failure of authorization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Apart from the failure of authorization, is it, and was it when taken, within the powers a corporation has under Subchapter II (powers)?
      `the act or transaction is void or voidable due to a failure of authorization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it void or voidable because of a failure of authorization?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the act a defective corporate act` IF
    `s 204(h)(1) the act is a defective corporate act` `the act is an overissue` `the act is an election or appointment of directors that is void or voidable due to a failure of authorization` `the act or transaction was purportedly taken by or on behalf of the corporation` `the act or transaction is, and when purportedly taken would have been, within the power of a corporation under subchapter II, ignoring the failure of authorization` `the act or transaction is void or voidable due to a failure of authorization`

-- src:716 | (2) “Failure of authorization” means: (i) the failure to authorize or effect an act or transaction in compliance with (A) the provisions of this title, (B) the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of the corporation, or (C) any plan or agreement to which the corporation is a party or the disclosure set forth in any proxy or consent solicitation statement, if and to the extent such failure would render such act or transaction void or voidable; or (ii) the failure of the board of directors or any officer of the corporation to authorize or approve any act or transaction taken by or on behalf of the corporation that would have required for its due authorization the approval of the board of directors or such officer;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(h)(2) (src:716)
@export Is there a failure of authorization (s 204(h)(2))?
GIVEN `the act failed to comply with the provisions of the Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the act fail to comply with the provisions of the Delaware General Corporation Law?
      `the act failed to comply with the certificate of incorporation or bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it fail to comply with the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws?
      `the act failed to comply with a plan or agreement of the corporation or with the disclosure in a proxy or consent solicitation statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it fail to comply with a plan or agreement to which the corporation is a party, or with the disclosure in a proxy or consent solicitation statement?
      `that failure would render the act void or voidable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would that failure make the act void or voidable?
      `the board of directors or an officer failed to authorize or approve an act that needed its approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the board of directors or an officer fail to authorize or approve an act that needed that approval to be duly authorized?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is there a failure of authorization` IF
    `s 204(h)(2) there is a failure of authorization` `the act failed to comply with the provisions of the Law` `the act failed to comply with the certificate of incorporation or bylaws` `the act failed to comply with a plan or agreement of the corporation or with the disclosure in a proxy or consent solicitation statement` `that failure would render the act void or voidable` `the board of directors or an officer failed to authorize or approve an act that needed its approval`

-- src:717 | (3) “Overissue” means the purported issuance of:
-- src:718 | a. Shares of capital stock of a class or series in excess of the number of shares of such class or series the corporation has the power to issue under § 161 of this title at the time of such issuance; or
-- src:719 | b. Shares of any class or series of capital stock that is not then authorized for issuance by the certificate of incorporation of the corporation;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(h)(3) (src:717-719)
@export Is the purported issue of shares an overissue (s 204(h)(3))?
GIVEN `the number of shares of the class or series purportedly issued` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of the class or series were purportedly issued?
      `the number of shares of that class or series the corporation had the power to issue under section 161 at the time` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of that class or series did the corporation have the power to issue under section 161 at the time?
      `the class or series was authorized for issuance by the certificate of incorporation at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the class or series authorized for issuance by the certificate of incorporation at the time?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the issue of shares an overissue` IF
    `s 204(h)(3) the purported issuance is an overissue` `the number of shares of the class or series purportedly issued` `the number of shares of that class or series the corporation had the power to issue under section 161 at the time` `the class or series was authorized for issuance by the certificate of incorporation at the time`

-- src:728 | (7) “Valid stock” means the shares of any class or series of capital stock of the corporation that have been duly authorized and validly issued in accordance with this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(h)(7) (src:728)
@export Are my shares valid stock (s 204(h)(7))?
GIVEN `my shares are shares of a class or series of capital stock of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they shares of a class or series of capital stock of the corporation?
      `my shares have been duly authorized in accordance with the Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have they been duly authorized in accordance with the Law?
      `my shares have been validly issued in accordance with the Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have they been validly issued in accordance with the Law?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my shares valid stock` IF
    `s 204(h)(7) the shares are valid stock` `my shares are shares of a class or series of capital stock of the corporation` `my shares have been duly authorized in accordance with the Law` `my shares have been validly issued in accordance with the Law`

-- src:720 | (4) “Putative stock” means the shares of any class or series of capital stock of the corporation (including shares issued upon exercise of options, rights, warrants or other securities convertible into shares of capital stock of the corporation, or interests with respect thereto that were created or issued pursuant to a defective corporate act) that:
-- src:721 | a. But for any failure of authorization, would constitute valid stock; or
-- src:722 | b. Cannot be determined by the board of directors to be valid stock;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(h)(4) (src:720-722)
@export Are my shares putative stock (s 204(h)(4))?
GIVEN `my shares are shares of capital stock of the corporation, including shares issued on exercise of options, rights, warrants or convertible securities, created or issued under a defective corporate act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they shares of capital stock of the corporation (including shares issued on exercise of options, rights, warrants or convertible securities, or interests in them, created or issued under a defective corporate act)?
      `but for a failure of authorization my shares would be valid stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc But for a failure of authorization, would they be valid stock?
      `the board of directors cannot determine that my shares are valid stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the board of directors cannot determine that they are valid stock?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my shares putative stock` IF
    `s 204(h)(4) the shares are putative stock` `my shares are shares of capital stock of the corporation, including shares issued on exercise of options, rights, warrants or convertible securities, created or issued under a defective corporate act` `but for a failure of authorization my shares would be valid stock` `the board of directors cannot determine that my shares are valid stock`

-- src:729 | In the absence of actual fraud in the transaction, the judgment of the board of directors that shares of stock are valid stock or putative stock shall be conclusive, unless otherwise determined by the Court of Chancery in a proceeding brought pursuant to § 205 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(h) (src:729)
@export Is the board's judgment that my shares are valid stock or putative stock conclusive (s 204(h), last sentence)? Returns the status that stands, or nothing if the text does not settle it.
GIVEN `the board of directors has made a judgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the board of directors made a judgment on whether the shares are valid stock or putative stock?
      `the board's judgment is that the shares are` IS A `s 204(h) Status of shares` @desc What is the board's judgment: that the shares are valid stock under section 204(h)(7), or putative stock under section 204(h)(4)? (ignored if there is no judgment)
      `there was actual fraud in the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there actual fraud in the transaction?
      `the Court of Chancery has determined the status` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court of Chancery determined the status of the shares in a proceeding under section 205?
      `the Court of Chancery determined that the shares are` IS A `s 204(h) Status of shares` @desc What did the Court determine: valid stock or putative stock? (ignored if it has not determined)
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 204(h) Status of shares`
DECIDE `Is the board's judgment on whether my shares are valid stock or putative stock conclusive` IS
    `s 204(h) the status of the shares that the board's judgment makes conclusive` boardJudgment `there was actual fraud in the transaction` courtDetermination
    WHERE
        boardJudgment MEANS IF `the board of directors has made a judgment` THEN JUST `the board's judgment is that the shares are` ELSE NOTHING
        courtDetermination MEANS IF `the Court of Chancery has determined the status` THEN JUST `the Court of Chancery determined that the shares are` ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 204(a) and (i) Am I protected, and is section 204 the only way?`

-- src:672 | (a) Subject to subsection (f) of this section, no defective corporate act or putative stock shall be void or voidable solely as a result of a failure of authorization if ratified as provided in this section or validated by the Court of Chancery in a proceeding brought under § 205 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(a) (src:672)
@export Is the defective corporate act or putative stock protected from being void or voidable solely for a failure of authorization (s 204(a))?
GIVEN `it was ratified as section 204 provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act or stock ratified as section 204 provides?
      `it was validated by the Court of Chancery in a proceeding under section 205` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it validated by the Court of Chancery in a proceeding under section 205?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the act or stock protected from being void or voidable solely for a failure of authorization` IF
    `s 204(a) the defective corporate act or putative stock is shielded from being void or voidable solely for a failure of authorization` `it was ratified as section 204 provides` `it was validated by the Court of Chancery in a proceeding under section 205`

-- src:730 | (i) Ratification under this section or validation under § 205 of this title shall not be deemed to be the exclusive means of ratifying or validating any act or transaction taken by or on behalf of the corporation, including any defective corporate act, or any issuance of stock, including any putative stock, or of adopting or endorsing any act or transaction taken by or in the name of the corporation prior to the commencement of its existence, and the absence or failure of ratification in accordance with either this section or validation under § 205 of this title shall not, of itself, affect the validity or effectiveness of any act or transaction or the issuance of any stock properly ratified under common law or otherwise, nor shall it create a presumption that any such act or transaction is or was a defective corporate act or that such stock is void or voidable.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(i) (src:730)
@export Is this means open to the corporation to ratify or validate an act, or to adopt or endorse one (s 204(i))?
GIVEN `the means` IS A `s 204(i) Means of ratifying, validating, adopting or endorsing` @desc Which means: ratification under section 204, validation under section 205, ratification under common law or otherwise, or adoption or endorsement of an act taken in the corporation's name before it began to exist?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this a way the corporation may ratify or validate` IF
    `s 204(i) the means is open to the corporation` `the means`

-- src:730 | (i) Ratification under this section or validation under § 205 of this title shall not be deemed to be the exclusive means of ratifying or validating any act or transaction taken by or on behalf of the corporation, including any defective corporate act, or any issuance of stock, including any putative stock, or of adopting or endorsing any act or transaction taken by or in the name of the corporation prior to the commencement of its existence, and the absence or failure of ratification in accordance with either this section or validation under § 205 of this title shall not, of itself, affect the validity or effectiveness of any act or transaction or the issuance of any stock properly ratified under common law or otherwise, nor shall it create a presumption that any such act or transaction is or was a defective corporate act or that such stock is void or voidable.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(i) (src:730)
@export If section 204 or 205 has not been used, does that of itself affect the validity of an act or stock that was properly ratified in another way (s 204(i))? Returns nothing for an act not so ratified.
GIVEN `the act or stock was properly ratified under common law or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act or stock properly ratified under common law or otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the lack of ratification of itself affect the validity of the act` IS
    `s 204(i) the absence or failure of ratification under s 204 or validation under s 205 of itself affects the validity of the act or stock` `the act or stock was properly ratified under common law or otherwise`

-- src:730 | (i) Ratification under this section or validation under § 205 of this title shall not be deemed to be the exclusive means of ratifying or validating any act or transaction taken by or on behalf of the corporation, including any defective corporate act, or any issuance of stock, including any putative stock, or of adopting or endorsing any act or transaction taken by or in the name of the corporation prior to the commencement of its existence, and the absence or failure of ratification in accordance with either this section or validation under § 205 of this title shall not, of itself, affect the validity or effectiveness of any act or transaction or the issuance of any stock properly ratified under common law or otherwise, nor shall it create a presumption that any such act or transaction is or was a defective corporate act or that such stock is void or voidable.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(i) (src:730)
@export Does the absence of ratification or validation create a presumption that the act is a defective corporate act, or that the stock is void or voidable (s 204(i))?
GIVEN `no ratification under section 204 or validation under section 205 has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has no ratification under section 204 or validation under section 205 been made?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the lack of ratification create a presumption that the act is defective` IF
    `s 204(i) the absence of ratification or validation creates a presumption that the act is a defective corporate act or that the stock is void or voidable` `no ratification under section 204 or validation under section 205 has been made`

§§ `s 204(b) and (c) The board's resolutions, and whether the stockholders must approve`

-- src:673 | (b) (1) In order to ratify 1 or more defective corporate acts pursuant to this section (other than the ratification of an election of the initial board of directors pursuant to paragraph (b)(2) of this section), the board of directors of the corporation shall adopt resolutions stating:
-- src:674 | (A) The defective corporate act or acts to be ratified;
-- src:675 | (B) The date of each defective corporate act or acts;
-- src:676 | (C) If such defective corporate act or acts involved the issuance of shares of putative stock, the number and type of shares of putative stock issued and the date or dates upon which such putative shares were purported to have been issued;
-- src:677 | (D) The nature of the failure of authorization in respect of each defective corporate act to be ratified; and
-- src:678 | (E) That the board of directors approves the ratification of the defective corporate act or acts.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(b)(1) (src:673-678)
@export Do the board's resolutions state what paragraphs (A) to (E) of section 204(b)(1) require?
GIVEN `the resolutions state the defective corporate act or acts to be ratified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the resolutions state the defective corporate act or acts to be ratified?
      `the resolutions state the date of each defective corporate act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they state the date of each defective corporate act?
      `the acts involved the issuance of shares of putative stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the acts involve the issuance of shares of putative stock?
      `the resolutions state the number and type of shares of putative stock issued and the dates they were purported to have been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, do they state the number and type of shares of putative stock issued and the date or dates they were purported to have been issued?
      `the resolutions state the nature of the failure of authorization in respect of each act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they state the nature of the failure of authorization in respect of each act?
      `the resolutions state that the board of directors approves the ratification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they state that the board of directors approves the ratification?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the board's resolutions state what section 204(b)(1) requires` IF
    `s 204(b)(1) the resolutions state what paragraphs (A) to (E) require` resolutions
    WHERE
        resolutions MEANS `s 204(b)(1) Board resolutions` WITH
            `the defective corporate act or acts to be ratified are stated` IS `the resolutions state the defective corporate act or acts to be ratified`
            `the date of each defective corporate act is stated` IS `the resolutions state the date of each defective corporate act`
            `the acts involved the issuance of shares of putative stock` IS `the acts involved the issuance of shares of putative stock`
            `the number and type of shares of putative stock issued and the date or dates they were purported to have been issued are stated` IS `the resolutions state the number and type of shares of putative stock issued and the dates they were purported to have been issued`
            `the nature of the failure of authorization in respect of each act is stated` IS `the resolutions state the nature of the failure of authorization in respect of each act`
            `the approval of the ratification by the board of directors is stated` IS `the resolutions state that the board of directors approves the ratification`

-- src:679 | The quorum and voting requirements applicable to the ratification by the board of directors of any defective corporate act shall be the quorum and voting requirements applicable to the type of defective corporate act proposed to be ratified at the time the board adopts the resolutions ratifying the defective corporate act; provided that if the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of the corporation, any plan or agreement to which the corporation was a party or any provision of this title, in each case as in effect as of the time of the defective corporate act, would have required a larger number or portion of directors or of specified directors for a quorum to be present or to approve the defective corporate act, such larger number or portion of such directors or such specified directors shall be required for a quorum to be present or to adopt the resolutions to ratify the defective corporate act, as applicable, except that the presence or approval of any director elected, appointed or nominated by holders of any class or series of which no shares are then outstanding, or by any person that is no longer a stockholder, shall not be required.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(b)(1) (src:679)
@export Did the board adopt the ratifying resolutions with the quorum and vote section 204(b)(1) requires?
GIVEN `directors needed for a quorum under the requirement that applies now` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors does the quorum requirement that applies to this type of act when the resolutions are adopted need?
      `directors needed to adopt under the requirement that applies now` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors does the voting requirement that applies to this type of act when the resolutions are adopted need?
      `directors needed for a quorum under the instruments in effect at the time of the act` IS A NUMBER @desc If the certificate, bylaws, a plan or agreement or the Law, as in effect at the time of the defective act, would have needed a larger number of directors for a quorum, how many? (otherwise the same number as above)
      `directors needed to adopt under the instruments in effect at the time of the act` IS A NUMBER @desc If they would have needed a larger number of directors to approve the act, how many? (otherwise the same number as above)
      `of those needed for a quorum, the number from an extinct class or a former stockholder` IS A NUMBER @desc Of the directors needed for a quorum under those instruments, how many were elected, appointed or nominated by a class or series of which no shares are now outstanding, or by a person who is no longer a stockholder?
      `of those needed to adopt, the number from an extinct class or a former stockholder` IS A NUMBER @desc Of the directors needed to approve under those instruments, how many were so elected, appointed or nominated?
      `the number of directors present` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors were present when the resolutions were adopted?
      `the number of directors who voted to adopt the resolutions` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors voted to adopt them?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did the board adopt the resolutions with the quorum and vote required` IF
    `s 204(b)(1) the board adopted the resolutions with the quorum and vote required` requirement `the number of directors present` `the number of directors who voted to adopt the resolutions`
    WHERE
        requirement MEANS `s 204(b)(1) Board requirement` WITH
            `directors needed for a quorum under the requirement that applies when the resolutions are adopted` IS `directors needed for a quorum under the requirement that applies now`
            `directors needed to adopt the resolutions under the requirement that applies when the resolutions are adopted` IS `directors needed to adopt under the requirement that applies now`
            `directors needed for a quorum under the instruments in effect at the time of the defective corporate act` IS `directors needed for a quorum under the instruments in effect at the time of the act`
            `directors needed to adopt the resolutions under the instruments in effect at the time of the defective corporate act` IS `directors needed to adopt under the instruments in effect at the time of the act`
            `of those needed for a quorum, the number elected, appointed or nominated by a class or series with no shares outstanding or by a person no longer a stockholder` IS `of those needed for a quorum, the number from an extinct class or a former stockholder`
            `of those needed to adopt, the number elected, appointed or nominated by a class or series with no shares outstanding or by a person no longer a stockholder` IS `of those needed to adopt, the number from an extinct class or a former stockholder`

-- src:679 | Such resolutions may also provide that, at any time before the validation effective time in respect of any defective corporate act set forth therein, notwithstanding the approval of the ratification of such defective corporate act by stockholders, the board of directors may abandon the ratification of such defective corporate act without further action of the stockholders. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(b)(1) (src:679)
@export May the board abandon the ratification without further action of the stockholders (s 204(b)(1))? Returns nothing if it is the same day as the validation effective time.
GIVEN `the resolutions provide that the board may abandon the ratification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the resolutions provide that, before the validation effective time, the board may abandon the ratification despite the stockholders' approval?
      `the day the board abandons the ratification` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the board abandon the ratification?
      `the day of the validation effective time` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the validation effective time?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the board abandon the ratification without further action of the stockholders` IS
    `s 204(b)(1) the resolutions' abandonment provision lets the board abandon the ratification without further action of the stockholders` `the resolutions provide that the board may abandon the ratification` `the day the board abandons the ratification` `the day of the validation effective time`

-- src:680 | (2) In order to ratify a defective corporate act in respect of the election of the initial board of directors of the corporation pursuant to § 108 of this title, a majority of the persons who, at the time the resolutions required by this paragraph (b)(2) of this section are adopted, are exercising the powers of directors under claim and color of an election or appointment as such may adopt resolutions stating:
-- src:681 | (A) The name of the person or persons who first took action in the name of the corporation as the initial board of directors of the corporation;
-- src:682 | (B) The earlier of the date on which such persons first took such action or were purported to have been elected as the initial board of directors; and
-- src:683 | (C) That the ratification of the election of such person or persons as the initial board of directors is approved.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(b)(2) (src:680-683)
@export May the persons exercising the powers of directors by these resolutions ratify the election of the initial board of directors (s 204(b)(2))? Returns nothing if the counts cannot be a vote.
GIVEN `the resolutions state the names of the persons who first took action as the initial board` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the resolutions state the names of the persons who first took action in the name of the corporation as the initial board of directors?
      `the resolutions state the earlier of the date they first took action and the date they were purported to have been elected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they state the earlier of the date those persons first took action and the date they were purported to have been elected?
      `the resolutions state that the ratification of their election as the initial board is approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they state that the ratification of their election as the initial board is approved?
      `the number of persons exercising the powers of directors under claim and color of an election or appointment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons are exercising the powers of directors under claim and color of an election or appointment as directors when the resolutions are adopted?
      `the number of those persons who adopt the resolutions` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them adopt the resolutions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the persons exercising the powers of directors ratify the election of the initial board` IS
    `s 204(b)(2) the persons may ratify the election of the initial board by these resolutions` resolutions `the number of persons exercising the powers of directors under claim and color of an election or appointment` `the number of those persons who adopt the resolutions`
    WHERE
        resolutions MEANS `s 204(b)(2) Initial board resolutions` WITH
            `the names of the persons who first took action in the name of the corporation as the initial board of directors are stated` IS `the resolutions state the names of the persons who first took action as the initial board`
            `the earlier of the date those persons first took action and the date they were purported to have been elected is stated` IS `the resolutions state the earlier of the date they first took action and the date they were purported to have been elected`
            `the approval of the ratification of their election as the initial board of directors is stated` IS `the resolutions state that the ratification of their election as the initial board is approved`

-- src:684 | (c) Each defective corporate act ratified pursuant to paragraph (b)(1) of this section shall be submitted to stockholders for approval as provided in subsection (d) of this section, unless:
-- src:685 | (1) (A) No other provision of this title, and no provision of the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of the corporation, or of any plan or agreement to which the corporation is a party, would have required stockholder approval of such defective corporate act to be ratified, either at the time of such defective corporate act or at the time the board of directors adopts the resolutions ratifying such defective corporate act pursuant to paragraph (b)(1) of this section; and
-- src:686 | (B) Such defective corporate act did not result from a failure to comply with § 203 of this title; or
-- src:687 | (2) As of the adoption of the resolutions of the board of directors adopted pursuant to paragraph (b)(1) of this section, there are no shares of valid stock outstanding and entitled to vote thereon, regardless of whether there then exist any shares of putative stock.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(c) (src:684-687)
@export Must the ratification be submitted to the stockholders for approval (s 204(c))?
GIVEN `the route` IS A `s 204(b) Route of ratification` @desc Is the board ratifying the election of the initial board of directors under section 204(b)(2), or any other defective corporate act under section 204(b)(1)?
      `no other provision of the Law, the certificate, the bylaws or a plan or agreement would have required stockholder approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would no other provision of the Law, the certificate of incorporation, the bylaws or a plan or agreement of the corporation have required stockholder approval of the act, either at the time of the act or when the board adopts the resolutions?
      `the act did not result from a failure to comply with section 203` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the act not result from a failure to comply with section 203 (business combinations with interested stockholders)?
      `there are no shares of valid stock outstanding and entitled to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When the board adopts the resolutions, are there no shares of valid stock outstanding and entitled to vote on the act (whether or not there are shares of putative stock)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the ratification be submitted to the stockholders for approval` IF
    `s 204(c) the ratification must be submitted to the stockholders for approval` `the route` `no other provision of the Law, the certificate, the bylaws or a plan or agreement would have required stockholder approval` `the act did not result from a failure to comply with section 203` `there are no shares of valid stock outstanding and entitled to vote`

§§ `s 204(d) The stockholders' meeting`

-- src:688 | If the ratification of a defective corporate act is required to be submitted to stockholders for approval pursuant to subsection (c) of this section, due notice of the time, place, if any, and purpose of the meeting shall be given at least 20 days before the date of the meeting to each holder of valid stock and putative stock, whether voting or nonvoting, at the address of such holder as it appears or most recently appeared, as appropriate, on the records of the corporation.
-- src:689 | (2) The notice shall also be given to the holders of record of valid stock and putative stock, whether voting or nonvoting, as of the time of the defective corporate act (or, in the case of any defective corporate act that involved the establishment of a record date for notice of or voting at any meeting of stockholders, for action by written consent of stockholders in lieu of a meeting, or for any other purpose, the record date for notice of or voting at such meeting, the record date for action by written consent, or the record date for such other action, as the case may be), other than holders whose identities or addresses cannot be determined from the records of the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(d)(1) (src:688); § 204(d)(2) (src:689)
@export Am I entitled to notice of the stockholders' meeting to approve the ratification (s 204(d)(1) and (2))?
GIVEN `I hold valid stock when notice is given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold valid stock (voting or nonvoting) when notice is given?
      `I hold putative stock when notice is given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold putative stock (voting or nonvoting) when notice is given?
      `I was a holder of record of valid or putative stock at the time of the defective corporate act or the record date it involved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a holder of record of valid stock or putative stock as of the time of the defective corporate act (or, if it involved a record date, that record date)?
      `my identity and address can be determined from the corporation's records` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can your identity and address be determined from the corporation's records?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to notice of the stockholders' meeting on the ratification` IF
    `s 204(d)(1) and (2) the holder is entitled to notice of the meeting` holder
    WHERE
        holder MEANS `s 204(d) Holder` WITH
            `holds valid stock when notice is given, whether voting or nonvoting` IS `I hold valid stock when notice is given`
            `holds putative stock when notice is given, whether voting or nonvoting` IS `I hold putative stock when notice is given`
            `was a holder of record of valid stock or putative stock as of the time of the defective corporate act or the record date it involved` IS `I was a holder of record of valid or putative stock at the time of the defective corporate act or the record date it involved`
            `the identity and address can be determined from the records of the corporation` IS `my identity and address can be determined from the corporation's records`

-- src:688 | due notice of the time, place, if any, and purpose of the meeting shall be given at least 20 days before the date of the meeting to each holder of valid stock and putative stock, whether voting or nonvoting, at the address of such holder as it appears or most recently appeared, as appropriate, on the records of the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(d)(1) (src:688)
@export Was notice of the stockholders' meeting given at least 20 days before it, and does it state the time, the place (if any) and the purpose (s 204(d)(1))?
GIVEN `the day notice of the meeting was given` IS A DATE @desc On what day was notice of the meeting given?
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the meeting?
      `the notice states the time of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the time of the meeting?
      `the meeting has a place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the meeting have a place (rather than being held solely by remote communication)?
      `the notice states the place of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is a place, does the notice state it?
      `the notice states the purpose of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the purpose of the meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was notice of the meeting given in time and in full` IF
    `s 204(d)(1) due notice of the meeting was given at least 20 days before it` notice
    WHERE
        notice MEANS `s 204(d) Meeting notice` WITH
            `the day notice of the meeting was given` IS `the day notice of the meeting was given`
            `the day of the meeting` IS `the day of the meeting`
            `the notice states the time of the meeting` IS `the notice states the time of the meeting`
            `the meeting has a place` IS `the meeting has a place`
            `the notice states the place of the meeting` IS `the notice states the place of the meeting`
            `the notice states the purpose of the meeting` IS `the notice states the purpose of the meeting`
            -- Placeholders: the rule called reads only the time, place, purpose and the two days.
            `the notice contains a copy of the resolutions adopted under paragraph (b)(1)` IS FALSE
            `the notice contains the information required by paragraphs (b)(1)(A) through (E)` IS FALSE
            `the notice contains the statement that a claim must be brought within 120 days from the applicable validation effective time` IS FALSE

-- src:690 | (3) The notice shall contain a copy of the resolutions adopted by the board of directors pursuant to paragraph (b)(1) of this section or the information required by paragraphs (b)(1)(A) through (E) of this section and a statement that any claim that the defective corporate act or putative stock ratified hereunder is void or voidable due to the failure of authorization, or that the Court of Chancery should declare in its discretion that a ratification in accordance with this section not be effective or be effective only on certain conditions must be brought within 120 days from the applicable validation effective time.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(d)(3) (src:690)
@export Does the notice of the stockholders' meeting contain what section 204(d)(3) requires?
GIVEN `the notice contains a copy of the resolutions the board adopted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice contain a copy of the resolutions the board adopted under section 204(b)(1)?
      `the notice contains the information required by paragraphs (b)(1)(A) through (E)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain the information required by paragraphs (b)(1)(A) through (E)?
      `the notice contains the statement of the 120-day limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain a statement that any claim that the act or stock is void or voidable, or that the Court should declare the ratification not effective or effective only on conditions, must be brought within 120 days from the applicable validation effective time?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the notice of the meeting contain what section 204(d)(3) requires` IF
    `s 204(d)(3) the notice contains what the paragraph requires` notice
    WHERE
        notice MEANS `s 204(d) Meeting notice` WITH
            -- Placeholders: the rule called reads only the three contents fields.
            `the day notice of the meeting was given` IS YearMonthDay 2000 1 1
            `the day of the meeting` IS YearMonthDay 2000 1 1
            `the notice states the time of the meeting` IS FALSE
            `the meeting has a place` IS FALSE
            `the notice states the place of the meeting` IS FALSE
            `the notice states the purpose of the meeting` IS FALSE
            `the notice contains a copy of the resolutions adopted under paragraph (b)(1)` IS `the notice contains a copy of the resolutions the board adopted`
            `the notice contains the information required by paragraphs (b)(1)(A) through (E)` IS `the notice contains the information required by paragraphs (b)(1)(A) through (E)`
            `the notice contains the statement that a claim must be brought within 120 days from the applicable validation effective time` IS `the notice contains the statement of the 120-day limit`

-- src:691 | (4) At such meeting, the quorum and voting requirements applicable to ratification of such defective corporate act shall be the quorum and voting requirements applicable to the type of defective corporate act proposed to be ratified at the time of the approval of the ratification, except that:
-- src:692 | a. If the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of the corporation, any plan or agreement to which the corporation was a party or any provision of this title in effect as of the time of the defective corporate act would have required a larger number or portion of stock or of any class or series thereof or of specified stockholders for a quorum to be present or to approve the defective corporate act, the presence or approval of such larger number or portion of stock or of such class or series thereof or of such specified stockholders shall be required for a quorum to be present or to approve the ratification of the defective corporate act, as applicable, except that the presence or approval of shares of any class or series of which no shares are then outstanding, or of any person that is no longer a stockholder, shall not be required;
-- src:693 | b. The approval by stockholders of the ratification of the election of a director shall require the affirmative vote of the majority of shares present at the meeting and entitled to vote on the election of such director, except that if the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of the corporation then in effect or in effect at the time of the defective election require or required a larger number or portion of stock or of any class or series thereof or of specified stockholders to elect such director, the affirmative vote of such larger number or portion of stock or of any class or series thereof or of such specified stockholders shall be required to ratify the election of such director, except that the presence or approval of shares of any class or series of which no shares are then outstanding, or of any person that is no longer a stockholder, shall not be required; and
-- src:694 | c. In the event of a failure of authorization resulting from failure to comply with the provisions of § 203 of this title, the ratification of the defective corporate act shall require the vote set forth in § 203(a)(3) of this title, regardless of whether such vote would have otherwise been required.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(d)(4) (src:691-694)
@export Did the stockholders approve the ratification with the quorum and vote required (s 204(d)(4))? Returns nothing if the director vote's counts cannot be a vote.
GIVEN `the quorum required for this type of act when the ratification is approved was present` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the quorum that applies to this type of act at the time of the approval present?
      `the vote required for this type of act when the ratification is approved was obtained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the vote that applies to this type of act at the time of the approval obtained? (not asked for the election of a director)
      `the defective corporate act is the election of a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act being ratified the election of a director?
      `the votes in favor of ratifying the election of the director` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many votes were cast in favor of ratifying the election of that director?
      `the votes present at the meeting and entitled to vote on the election of the director` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were present at the meeting and entitled to vote on the election of that director?
      `the instruments in effect at the time of the act required a larger quorum or vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the certificate, bylaws, a plan or agreement or the Law, as in effect at the time of the defective act, have required a larger quorum or vote (of stock, of a class or series, or of specified stockholders)?
      `that larger quorum and vote were obtained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, were they obtained, leaving out shares of a class or series with no shares outstanding and any person no longer a stockholder?
      `the failure of authorization resulted from a failure to comply with section 203` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the failure of authorization result from a failure to comply with section 203?
      `the vote set forth in section 203(a)(3) was obtained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, was the vote set forth in section 203(a)(3) obtained?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did the stockholders approve the ratification` IS
    `s 204(d)(4) the stockholders approved the ratification` facts directorVote
    WHERE
        facts MEANS `s 204(d)(4) Approval facts` WITH
            `the quorum required for this type of act when the ratification is approved was present` IS `the quorum required for this type of act when the ratification is approved was present`
            `the vote required for this type of act when the ratification is approved was obtained` IS `the vote required for this type of act when the ratification is approved was obtained`
            `the defective corporate act is the election of a director` IS `the defective corporate act is the election of a director`
            `the instruments in effect at the time of the defective corporate act required a larger quorum or vote` IS `the instruments in effect at the time of the act required a larger quorum or vote`
            `that larger quorum and vote were obtained, leaving out shares of a class or series with no shares outstanding and any person no longer a stockholder` IS `that larger quorum and vote were obtained`
            `the failure of authorization resulted from a failure to comply with s 203` IS `the failure of authorization resulted from a failure to comply with section 203`
            `the vote set forth in s 203(a)(3) was obtained` IS `the vote set forth in section 203(a)(3) was obtained`
        directorVote MEANS `s 204(d)(4)b. the ratification of the election of the director carries by a majority of the votes present` `the votes in favor of ratifying the election of the director` `the votes present at the meeting and entitled to vote on the election of the director`

-- src:695 | (5) Shares of putative stock as of the adoption by the board of directors of resolutions pursuant to paragraph (b)(1) of this section (and without giving effect to any ratification that becomes effective after such adoption) shall neither be entitled to vote nor counted for quorum purposes in any vote to ratify any defective corporate act.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(d)(5) (src:695)
@export Are my shares entitled to vote, and counted for a quorum, in the vote to ratify (s 204(d)(5))? Returns nothing if they were not putative stock when the board adopted the resolutions.
GIVEN `my shares were putative stock when the board adopted the resolutions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were your shares putative stock when the board adopted the resolutions, without giving effect to any ratification that becomes effective after that?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my putative shares vote on the ratification` IS
    `s 204(d)(5) the shares are entitled to vote and are counted for a quorum in the vote to ratify` `my shares were putative stock when the board adopted the resolutions`

§§ `s 204(e) The certificate of validation`

-- src:696 | (e) (1) If a defective corporate act ratified pursuant to this section would have required under any other section of this title the filing of a certificate in accordance with § 103 of this title, and either (i) such certificate requires any change to give effect to the defective corporate act in accordance with this section (including a change to the date and time of the effectiveness of such certificate) or (ii) a certificate was not previously filed under § 103 of this title in respect of the defective corporate act, then, in lieu of filing the certificate otherwise required by this title, the corporation shall file a certificate of validation with respect to such defective corporate act in accordance with § 103 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(e)(1) (src:696)
@export Must the corporation file a certificate of validation in lieu of the certificate the other section requires (s 204(e)(1))?
GIVEN `the act would have required a certificate under section 103` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the ratified act have required, under another section of the Law, the filing of a certificate in accordance with section 103?
      `that certificate requires a change to give effect to the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that certificate require any change to give effect to the act under section 204 (including the date and time it takes effect)?
      `no certificate was previously filed under section 103` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was no certificate previously filed under section 103 for the act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation file a certificate of validation` IF
    `s 204(e)(1) the corporation must file a certificate of validation in lieu of the certificate the other section requires` `the act would have required a certificate under section 103` `that certificate requires a change to give effect to the act` `no certificate was previously filed under section 103`

-- src:697 | (2) A separate certificate of validation shall be required for each defective corporate act requiring the filing of a certificate of validation under this section, except that (i) 2 or more defective corporate acts may be included in a single certificate of validation if the corporation filed, or to comply with this title would have filed, a single certificate under another provision of this title to effect such acts, and (ii) 2 or more overissues of shares of any class, classes or series of stock may be included in a single certificate of validation, provided that the increase in the number of authorized shares of each such class or series set forth in the certificate of validation shall be effective as of the date of the first such overissue.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(e)(2) (src:697)
@export Does each of two or more defective acts need its own certificate of validation (s 204(e)(2))?
GIVEN `a single certificate was filed, or would have been filed, under another provision to effect all the acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation file, or would it to comply with the Law have filed, a single certificate under another provision of the Law to effect all the acts?
      `the acts are all overissues of shares of a class, classes or series of stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the acts all overissues of shares of a class, classes or series of stock?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does each of several defective acts need its own certificate of validation` IF
    `s 204(e)(2) each of two or more acts needs its own certificate of validation` `a single certificate was filed, or would have been filed, under another provision to effect all the acts` `the acts are all overissues of shares of a class, classes or series of stock`

-- src:697 | (2) A separate certificate of validation shall be required for each defective corporate act requiring the filing of a certificate of validation under this section, except that (i) 2 or more defective corporate acts may be included in a single certificate of validation if the corporation filed, or to comply with this title would have filed, a single certificate under another provision of this title to effect such acts, and (ii) 2 or more overissues of shares of any class, classes or series of stock may be included in a single certificate of validation, provided that the increase in the number of authorized shares of each such class or series set forth in the certificate of validation shall be effective as of the date of the first such overissue.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(e)(2) (src:697)
@export In a certificate of validation covering several overissues, as of what date is the increase in authorized shares effective (s 204(e)(2)(ii))? That is the date of the first overissue.
GIVEN `the dates of the overissues` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On what dates were the overissues?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `As of what date is the increase in authorized shares effective in a combined certificate` IS
    `s 204(e)(2)(ii) the date of the first overissue` `the dates of the overissues`

-- src:698 | (3) The certificate of validation shall set forth:
-- src:699 | a. That the corporation has ratified 1 or more defective corporate acts that would have required the filing of a certificate under § 103 of this title;
-- src:700 | b. That each such defective corporate act has been ratified in accordance with this section; and
-- src:701 | c. The information required by 1 of the following paragraphs:
-- src:702 | 1. If a certificate was previously filed under § 103 of this title in respect of the defective corporate act and such certificate requires any change to give effect to the defective corporate act in accordance with this section (including a change to the date and time of the effectiveness of such certificate), the certificate of validation shall set forth:
-- src:703 | A. The name, title and filing date of the certificate so previously filed and of any certificate of correction thereto;
-- src:704 | B. A statement that a certificate containing all of the information required to be included under the applicable section or sections of this title to give effect to the defective corporate act is attached as an exhibit to the certificate of validation; and
-- src:705 | C. The date and time that such certificate shall be deemed to have become effective pursuant to this section; or
-- src:706 | 2. If a certificate was not previously filed under § 103 of this title in respect of the defective corporate act and the defective corporate act ratified pursuant to this section would have required under any other section of this title the filing of a certificate in accordance with § 103 of this title, the certificate of validation shall set forth:
-- src:707 | A. A statement that a certificate containing all of the information required to be included under the applicable section or sections of this title to give effect to the defective corporate act is attached as an exhibit to the certificate of validation, and
-- src:708 | B. The date and time that such certificate shall be deemed to have become effective pursuant to this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(e)(3) (src:698-708)
@export Does the certificate of validation set forth what section 204(e)(3) requires?
GIVEN `it sets forth that the corporation has ratified defective corporate acts that would have required a certificate under section 103` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set forth that the corporation has ratified one or more defective corporate acts that would have required the filing of a certificate under section 103?
      `it sets forth that each act has been ratified in accordance with section 204` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set forth that each such act has been ratified in accordance with section 204?
      `a certificate was previously filed under section 103 and requires a change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a certificate previously filed under section 103 for the act, and does it require a change to give effect to the act?
      `it sets forth the name, title and filing date of the certificate previously filed and of any certificate of correction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does it set forth the name, title and filing date of the certificate previously filed and of any certificate of correction?
      `it sets forth that a certificate with all the required information is attached as an exhibit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set forth that a certificate containing all the information required to give effect to the act is attached as an exhibit?
      `it sets forth the date and time the certificate is deemed to have become effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set forth the date and time the certificate is deemed to have become effective?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the certificate of validation set forth what section 204(e)(3) requires` IF
    `s 204(e)(3) the certificate of validation sets forth what the paragraph requires` certificate
    WHERE
        certificate MEANS `s 204(e)(3) Certificate of validation` WITH
            `it sets forth that the corporation has ratified 1 or more defective corporate acts that would have required the filing of a certificate under s 103` IS `it sets forth that the corporation has ratified defective corporate acts that would have required a certificate under section 103`
            `it sets forth that each such defective corporate act has been ratified in accordance with this section` IS `it sets forth that each act has been ratified in accordance with section 204`
            `a certificate was previously filed under s 103 in respect of the act and requires a change to give effect to it` IS `a certificate was previously filed under section 103 and requires a change`
            `it sets forth the name, title and filing date of the certificate previously filed and of any certificate of correction` IS `it sets forth the name, title and filing date of the certificate previously filed and of any certificate of correction`
            `it sets forth that a certificate containing all the information required is attached as an exhibit` IS `it sets forth that a certificate with all the required information is attached as an exhibit`
            `it sets forth the date and time the certificate shall be deemed to have become effective` IS `it sets forth the date and time the certificate is deemed to have become effective`

-- src:709 | (4) A certificate attached to a certificate of validation need not be separately executed and acknowledged and need not include any statement required by any other section of this title that such instrument has been approved and adopted in accordance with the provisions of such other section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(e)(4) (src:709)
@export Must a certificate attached to a certificate of validation be separately executed and acknowledged, or carry a statement of approval and adoption (s 204(e)(4))? Returns nothing for any other instrument.
GIVEN `the instrument is a certificate attached to a certificate of validation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument a certificate attached to a certificate of validation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the certificate attached to a certificate of validation be separately executed and acknowledged` IS
    `s 204(e)(4) the attached certificate must be separately executed and acknowledged or carry the statement of approval and adoption` `the instrument is a certificate attached to a certificate of validation`

§§ `s 204(f) and (h)(6) When the ratification takes effect`

-- src:724 | (6) “Validation effective time,” with respect to any defective corporate act ratified pursuant to this section, means the latest of:
-- src:725 | a. The time at which the defective corporate act submitted to the stockholders for approval pursuant to subsection (c) of this section is approved by such stockholders or if no such vote of stockholders is required to approve the ratification of the defective corporate act, immediately following the time at which the board of directors adopts the resolutions required by paragraph (b)(1) or (b)(2) of this section;
-- src:726 | b. Where no certificate of validation is required to be filed pursuant to subsection (e) of this section, the time, if any, specified by the board of directors in the resolutions adopted pursuant to paragraph (b)(1) or (b)(2) of this section, which time shall not precede the time at which such resolutions are adopted; and
-- src:727 | c. The time at which any certificate of validation filed pursuant to subsection (e) of this section shall become effective in accordance with § 103 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(h)(6) (src:724-727)
@export On what day is the validation effective time (s 204(h)(6))? Returns nothing while a component is still to come, or if a time the board specified precedes the adoption of its resolutions.
GIVEN `a stockholder vote is required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 204(c) require the stockholders' approval?
      `the stockholders have approved the ratification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the stockholders approved the ratification? (ignore if no vote is required)
      `the day the stockholders approved the ratification` IS A DATE @desc On what day did they approve it? (ignored if they have not)
      `the day the board adopted the resolutions` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the board adopt the resolutions?
      `a certificate of validation is required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 204(e) require a certificate of validation?
      `the board specified a time in the resolutions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the board specify a time for the ratification to take effect in the resolutions? (only counts if no certificate of validation is required)
      `the day the board specified` IS A DATE @desc On what day? (ignored if it specified none)
      `the certificate of validation has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the certificate of validation become effective under section 103?
      `the day the certificate of validation became effective` IS A DATE @desc On what day? (ignored if it has not)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day is the validation effective time` IS
    `s 204(h)(6) the day of the validation effective time`
        (`s 204(h)(6)a. the time at which the stockholders approve or the board adopts the resolutions` `a stockholder vote is required` approvalDay `the day the board adopted the resolutions`)
        (`s 204(h)(6)b. the time the board specified in the resolutions` `a certificate of validation is required` boardDay `the day the board adopted the resolutions`)
        (`s 204(h)(6)c. the time the certificate of validation becomes effective` `a certificate of validation is required` certificateDay)
    WHERE
        approvalDay MEANS IF `the stockholders have approved the ratification` THEN JUST `the day the stockholders approved the ratification` ELSE NOTHING
        boardDay MEANS IF `the board specified a time in the resolutions` THEN JUST `the day the board specified` ELSE NOTHING
        certificateDay MEANS IF `the certificate of validation has become effective` THEN JUST `the day the certificate of validation became effective` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:672 | Subject to subsection (f) of this section, no defective corporate act or putative stock shall be void or voidable solely as a result of a failure of authorization if ratified as provided in this section …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(a) (src:672); § 204(b)(1) (src:679); § 204(c) (src:684); § 204(e)(1) (src:696)
@export Has the defective corporate act been ratified in accordance with section 204? Returns nothing if the stockholders' approval is not covered.
GIVEN `the resolutions state what the route requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the board's resolutions state what section 204(b) requires?
      `the board adopted the resolutions with the quorum and vote required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the board adopt them with the quorum and vote required?
      `the board abandoned the ratification before the validation effective time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the board abandon the ratification before the validation effective time?
      `the ratification must be submitted to the stockholders for approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Must the ratification be submitted to the stockholders for approval under section 204(c)?
      `the stockholders have approved the ratification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, have the stockholders approved it?
      `the stockholders' approval is covered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the stockholders' approval be worked out from the counts (answer no if the count of votes cannot be a vote)?
      `a certificate of validation is required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a certificate of validation required?
      `the certificate of validation was executed, acknowledged and filed and sets forth what is required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, was it executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with section 103, and does it set forth what section 204(e)(3) requires?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the defective corporate act been ratified in accordance with section 204` IS
    `s 204 the defective corporate act has been ratified in accordance with this section` `the resolutions state what the route requires` `the board adopted the resolutions with the quorum and vote required` `the board abandoned the ratification before the validation effective time` `the ratification must be submitted to the stockholders for approval` approved `a certificate of validation is required` `the certificate of validation was executed, acknowledged and filed and sets forth what is required`
    WHERE
        approved MEANS IF `the stockholders' approval is covered` THEN JUST `the stockholders have approved the ratification` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:710 | (f) From and after the validation effective time, unless otherwise determined in an action brought pursuant to § 205 of this title:
-- src:711 | (1) Subject to the last sentence of subsection (d) of this section, each defective corporate act ratified in accordance with this section shall no longer be deemed void or voidable as a result of the failure of authorization described in the resolutions adopted pursuant to subsection (b) of this section and such effect shall be retroactive to the time of the defective corporate act; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(f)(1) (src:710-711)
@export From and after the validation effective time, is the ratified act no longer deemed void or voidable as a result of the failure of authorization described in the resolutions (s 204(f)(1))? Returns nothing on the same day as the validation effective time.
GIVEN `the defective corporate act was ratified in accordance with section 204` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the defective corporate act ratified in accordance with section 204?
      `the Court of Chancery has determined otherwise in an action under section 205` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court of Chancery determined otherwise in an action under section 205?
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc For what day are you asking?
      `the day of the validation effective time` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the validation effective time?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the ratified act no longer void or voidable` IS
    `s 204(f)(1) the ratified act is no longer deemed void or voidable as a result of the failure of authorization described in the resolutions` `the defective corporate act was ratified in accordance with section 204` `the Court of Chancery has determined otherwise in an action under section 205` `the day in question` `the day of the validation effective time`

-- src:711 | (1) Subject to the last sentence of subsection (d) of this section, each defective corporate act ratified in accordance with this section shall no longer be deemed void or voidable as a result of the failure of authorization described in the resolutions adopted pursuant to subsection (b) of this section and such effect shall be retroactive to the time of the defective corporate act; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(f)(1) (src:711)
@export To what date is the effect of the ratification retroactive (s 204(f)(1))? It is the time of the defective corporate act.
GIVEN `the date the defective corporate act was purported to have been taken` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the defective corporate act purported to have been taken?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `As of what date is the effect of the ratification retroactive` IS
    `s 204(f)(1) the date to which the effect of the ratification is retroactive` `the date the defective corporate act was purported to have been taken`

-- src:712 | (2) Subject to the last sentence of subsection (d) of this section, each share or fraction of a share of putative stock issued or purportedly issued pursuant to any such defective corporate act shall no longer be deemed void or voidable and shall be deemed to be an identical share or fraction of a share of outstanding stock as of the time it was purportedly issued.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(f)(2) (src:712)
@export From and after the validation effective time, is my share of putative stock no longer deemed void or voidable and deemed an identical outstanding share (s 204(f)(2))? Returns nothing on the same day as the validation effective time.
GIVEN `my share was issued or purportedly issued under a defective corporate act ratified in accordance with section 204` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your share issued or purportedly issued under a defective corporate act ratified in accordance with section 204?
      `the Court of Chancery has determined otherwise in an action under section 205` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court of Chancery determined otherwise in an action under section 205?
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc For what day are you asking?
      `the day of the validation effective time` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the validation effective time?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my putative share now an identical outstanding share` IS
    `s 204(f)(2) the share of putative stock is no longer deemed void or voidable and is deemed an identical outstanding share` `my share was issued or purportedly issued under a defective corporate act ratified in accordance with section 204` `the Court of Chancery has determined otherwise in an action under section 205` `the day in question` `the day of the validation effective time`

-- src:712 | (2) Subject to the last sentence of subsection (d) of this section, each share or fraction of a share of putative stock issued or purportedly issued pursuant to any such defective corporate act shall no longer be deemed void or voidable and shall be deemed to be an identical share or fraction of a share of outstanding stock as of the time it was purportedly issued.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(f)(2) (src:712)
@export As of what date is my share of putative stock deemed an identical outstanding share (s 204(f)(2))? It is the time it was purportedly issued.
GIVEN `the date my share was purportedly issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your share purportedly issued?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `As of what date is my putative share deemed outstanding` IS
    `s 204(f)(2) the date as of which the share is deemed an identical outstanding share` `the date my share was purportedly issued`

§§ `s 204(g) Notice of the board's ratification`

-- src:713 | In respect of each defective corporate act ratified by the board of directors pursuant to subsection (b) of this section, prompt notice of the ratification shall be given to all holders of valid stock and putative stock, whether voting or nonvoting, as of the date the board of directors adopts the resolutions approving such defective corporate act, or as of a date within 60 days after such date of adoption, as established by the board of directors, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(g) (src:713)
@export Is the day the board established for determining who is given notice of the ratification the day it adopted the resolutions or a day within 60 days after it (s 204(g))?
GIVEN `the day the board adopts the resolutions` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the board adopt the resolutions?
      `the day the board establishes` IS A DATE @desc What day did the board establish for determining the holders to be given notice?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the day the board set for the notice record date permitted` IF
    `s 204(g) the day the board establishes is the day the board adopts the resolutions or a day within 60 days after it` `the day the board adopts the resolutions` `the day the board establishes`

-- src:713 | The notice shall also be given to the holders of record of valid stock and putative stock, whether voting or nonvoting, as of the time of the defective corporate act, other than holders whose identities or addresses cannot be determined from the records of the corporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(g) (src:713)
@export Am I owed notice of the board's ratification under section 204(g)?
GIVEN `I hold valid or putative stock as of the day established for this notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold valid stock or putative stock, voting or nonvoting, as of the date the board adopted the resolutions or the date within 60 days after it that the board established?
      `I was a holder of record of valid or putative stock as of the time of the defective corporate act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a holder of record of valid stock or putative stock as of the time of the defective corporate act?
      `my identity and address can be determined from the corporation's records` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can your identity and address be determined from the corporation's records?
      `I approved the action by consent in lieu of a meeting under section 228` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you approve the action by written consent in lieu of a meeting under section 228?
      `I hold putative stock and otherwise consented to the action in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold putative stock and did you otherwise consent to the action in writing?
      `notice of the ratification is to be given in accordance with subsection (d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is notice of the ratification to be given to you as notice of the stockholders' meeting under subsection (d)?
      `the notice is included in a notice required under section 228(e)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice included in a notice required under section 228(e)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I owed notice of the board's ratification` IF
    `s 204(g) the holder is owed this notice` holder `notice of the ratification is to be given in accordance with subsection (d)` `the notice is included in a notice required under section 228(e)`
    WHERE
        holder MEANS `s 204(g) Holder` WITH
            `holds valid stock or putative stock, voting or nonvoting, as of the day established for this notice` IS `I hold valid or putative stock as of the day established for this notice`
            `was a holder of record of valid stock or putative stock as of the time of the defective corporate act` IS `I was a holder of record of valid or putative stock as of the time of the defective corporate act`
            `the holder's identity and address can be determined from the records of the corporation` IS `my identity and address can be determined from the corporation's records`
            `the holder approved the action by consent in lieu of a meeting under s 228` IS `I approved the action by consent in lieu of a meeting under section 228`
            `the holder holds putative stock and otherwise consented to the action in writing` IS `I hold putative stock and otherwise consented to the action in writing`

-- src:713 | prompt notice of the ratification shall be given to all holders of valid stock and putative stock, whether voting or nonvoting, as of the date the board of directors adopts the resolutions approving such defective corporate act, or as of a date within 60 days after such date of adoption, as established by the board of directors, at the address of such holder as it appears or most recently appeared, as appropriate, on the records of the corporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(g) (src:713)
@export Has the corporation done what section 204(g) requires of it toward me?
GIVEN `I am owed this notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you owed notice of the board's ratification (see the question above)?
      `the corporation has a class of stock listed on a national securities exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation have a class of stock listed on a national securities exchange?
      `the ratification is disclosed in a public filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the ratification disclosed in a document the corporation publicly filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission under section 13, 14 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 (or the corresponding later provisions)?
      `I was given notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you given notice?
      `the notice was given promptly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it given promptly?
      `the notice contains a copy of the resolutions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice contain a copy of the resolutions the board adopted?
      `the notice contains the information required by paragraphs (b)(1)(A) to (E) or (b)(2)(A) to (C)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain the information specified in paragraphs (b)(1)(A) through (E) or (b)(2)(A) through (C), as applicable?
      `the notice contains the statement of the 120-day limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain a statement that any claim must be brought within 120 days from the later of the validation effective time and the time the notice is given?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the corporation done what section 204(g) requires for me` IF
    `s 204(g) the corporation has done what the subsection requires for the holder` `I am owed this notice` deemed `I was given notice` `the notice was given promptly` contents
    WHERE
        deemed MEANS `s 204(g) the notice required by this subsection and by subsection (d) may be deemed given` `the corporation has a class of stock listed on a national securities exchange` `the ratification is disclosed in a public filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission`
        contents MEANS `s 204(g) the notice contains what the subsection requires` `the notice contains a copy of the resolutions` `the notice contains the information required by paragraphs (b)(1)(A) to (E) or (b)(2)(A) to (C)` `the notice contains the statement of the 120-day limit`

-- src:713 | Solely for purposes of subsection (d) of this section and this subsection, notice to holders of putative stock, and notice to holders of valid stock and putative stock as of the time of the defective corporate act, shall be treated as notice to holders of valid stock for purposes of §§ 222 and 228, 229, 230, 232 and 233 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(g) (src:713)
@export Is notice to me treated as notice to a holder of valid stock for the purposes of sections 222, 228, 229, 230, 232 and 233 (s 204(g), last sentence)? Returns nothing unless I am a holder of putative stock or a holder as of the time of the act.
GIVEN `I am a holder of putative stock, or a holder as of the time of the defective corporate act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a holder of putative stock, or a holder as of the time of the defective corporate act?
      `the purpose is subsection (d) or (g) of section 204` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose subsection (d) or (g) of section 204 (the section's own notices)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the notice to me treated as notice to a holder of valid stock` IS
    `s 204(g) the notice is treated as notice to a holder of valid stock for the purposes of ss 222, 228, 229, 230, 232 and 233` `I am a holder of putative stock, or a holder as of the time of the defective corporate act` `the purpose is subsection (d) or (g) of section 204`

§§ `s 205 Going to the Court of Chancery`

-- src:734 | (a) Subject to subsection (f) of this section, upon application by the corporation, any successor entity to the corporation, any member of the board of directors, any record or beneficial holder of valid stock or putative stock, any record or beneficial holder of valid or putative stock as of the time of a defective corporate act ratified pursuant to § 204 of this title, or any other person claiming to be substantially and adversely affected by a ratification pursuant to § 204 of this title, the Court of Chancery may:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(a) (src:734)
@export Am I among those who may apply to the Court of Chancery under section 205(a) about the validity of a defective corporate act or stock?
GIVEN `I am the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the corporation?
      `I am a successor entity to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a successor entity to the corporation?
      `I am a member of the board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the board of directors?
      `I am a record or beneficial holder of valid stock or putative stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a record or beneficial holder of valid stock or putative stock?
      `I was a record or beneficial holder of valid or putative stock as of the time of a defective corporate act ratified under section 204` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a record or beneficial holder of valid or putative stock as of the time of a defective corporate act ratified under section 204?
      `I claim to be substantially and adversely affected by a ratification under section 204` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you claim to be substantially and adversely affected by a ratification under section 204?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I among those who may apply to the Court of Chancery under section 205` IF
    `s 205(a) the person is among those who may apply to the Court of Chancery` applicant
    WHERE
        applicant MEANS `s 205(a) Applicant` WITH
            `the corporation` IS `I am the corporation`
            `a successor entity to the corporation` IS `I am a successor entity to the corporation`
            `a member of the board of directors` IS `I am a member of the board of directors`
            `a record or beneficial holder of valid stock or putative stock` IS `I am a record or beneficial holder of valid stock or putative stock`
            `a record or beneficial holder of valid or putative stock as of the time of a defective corporate act ratified under s 204` IS `I was a record or beneficial holder of valid or putative stock as of the time of a defective corporate act ratified under section 204`
            `a person claiming to be substantially and adversely affected by a ratification under s 204` IS `I claim to be substantially and adversely affected by a ratification under section 204`

-- src:735 | (1) Determine the validity and effectiveness of any defective corporate act ratified pursuant to § 204 of this title;
-- src:736 | (2) Determine the validity and effectiveness of the ratification of any defective corporate act pursuant to § 204 of this title;
-- src:737 | (3) Determine the validity and effectiveness of any defective corporate act not ratified or not ratified effectively pursuant to § 204 of this title;
-- src:738 | (4) Determine the validity of any corporate act or transaction and any stock, rights or options to acquire stock; and
-- src:739 | (5) Modify or waive any of the procedures set forth in § 204 of this title to ratify a defective corporate act.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(a) (src:734-739)
@export May the Court of Chancery determine this matter on my application under section 205(a)?
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `s 205(a) Matter the Court may determine` @desc Which matter do you want the Court to determine?
      `a person among those who may apply has applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a person among those who may apply under section 205(a) applied?
      `a ratification of the act was made under section 204` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a ratification of the act made under section 204?
      `that ratification was effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that ratification effective?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `What may the Court of Chancery determine on my application` IF
    `s 205(a) the Court of Chancery may determine the matter on the application` `the matter` `a person among those who may apply has applied` `a ratification of the act was made under section 204` `that ratification was effective`

-- src:762 | may be brought after the expiration of 120 days from the later of the validation effective time and the time notice, if any, that is required to be given pursuant to § 204(g) of this title is given with respect to such ratification, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(f) (src:759-762)
@export By what day must an action of the kinds section 205(f) limits be brought? It is 120 days after the later of the validation effective time and the time notice under section 204(g) is given. Returns nothing while that notice is required and not yet given.
GIVEN `the day of the validation effective time` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the validation effective time?
      `notice is required to be given under section 204(g)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is notice of the ratification required to be given under section 204(g)?
      `that notice has been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been given?
      `the day that notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what day was it given? (ignored if it has not been)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I bring an action under section 205` IS
    `s 205(f) the last day to bring an action of the kinds the subsection limits` `the day of the validation effective time` `notice is required to be given under section 204(g)` noticeDay
    WHERE
        noticeDay MEANS IF `that notice has been given` THEN JUST `the day that notice was given` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:759 | (f) Notwithstanding any other provision of this section, no action asserting:
-- src:760 | (1) That a defective corporate act or putative stock ratified in accordance with § 204 of this title is void or voidable due to a failure of authorization identified in the resolution adopted in accordance with 204(b) of this title; or
-- src:761 | (2) That the Court of Chancery should declare in its discretion that a ratification in accordance with § 204 of this title not be effective or be effective only on certain conditions,
-- src:762 | may be brought after the expiration of 120 days from the later of the validation effective time and the time notice, if any, that is required to be given pursuant to § 204(g) of this title is given with respect to such ratification, except that this subsection shall not apply to an action asserting that a ratification was not accomplished in accordance with § 204 of this title or to any person to whom notice of the ratification was required to have been given pursuant to § 204(d) or (g) of this title, but to whom such notice was not given.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(f) (src:759-762)
@export Is my action barred by the 120-day limit in section 205(f)?
GIVEN `the kind of claim` IS A `s 205(f) Kind of claim` @desc What does the action assert: that a ratified act or stock is void or voidable for a failure of authorization identified in the resolution; that the Court should declare the ratification not effective or effective only on conditions; that a ratification was not accomplished in accordance with section 204; or something else?
      `I was required to be given notice under section 204(d) or (g) and was not given it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you required to be given notice of the ratification under section 204(d) or (g) and were not given it?
      `there is a last day to bring the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the 120-day period begun, so that there is a last day (see the question above)?
      `the last day to bring the action` IS A DATE @desc What is that last day? (ignored if the period has not begun)
      `the day the action is brought` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you bring the action?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my action barred by the 120-day limit` IF
    `s 205(f) the action is barred by this subsection` `the kind of claim` `I was required to be given notice under section 204(d) or (g) and was not given it` lastDay `the day the action is brought`
    WHERE
        lastDay MEANS IF `there is a last day to bring the action` THEN JUST `the last day to bring the action` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:734 | (a) Subject to subsection (f) of this section, upon application by the corporation, any successor entity to the corporation, any member of the board of directors, any record or beneficial holder of valid stock or putative stock, any record or beneficial holder of valid or putative stock as of the time of a defective corporate act ratified pursuant to § 204 of this title, or any other person claiming to be substantially and adversely affected by a ratification pursuant to § 204 of this title, the Court of Chancery may:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(a) (src:734); § 205(f) (src:759-762)
@export May I bring the action, being among those who may apply and not barred by the 120-day limit (s 205(a) and (f))?
GIVEN `I am among those who may apply under section 205(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you among those who may apply under section 205(a)?
      `my action is barred by the 120-day limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your action barred by the 120-day limit in section 205(f)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I bring the action` IF
    `s 205(a) the person may bring the action` `I am among those who may apply under section 205(a)` `my action is barred by the 120-day limit`

-- src:740 | (b) In connection with an action under this section, the Court of Chancery may:
-- src:741 | (1) Declare that a ratification in accordance with and pursuant to § 204 of this title is not effective or shall only be effective at a time or upon conditions established by the Court;
-- src:742 | (2) Validate and declare effective any defective corporate act or putative stock and impose conditions upon such validation by the Court;
-- src:743 | (3) Require measures to remedy or avoid harm to any person substantially and adversely affected by a ratification pursuant to § 204 of this title or from any order of the Court pursuant to this section, excluding any harm that would have resulted if the defective corporate act had been valid when approved or effectuated;
-- src:744 | (4) Order the Secretary of State to accept an instrument for filing with an effective time specified by the Court, which effective time may be prior or subsequent to the time of such order, provided that the filing date of such instrument shall be determined in accordance with § 103(c)(3) of this title;
-- src:745 | (5) Approve a stock ledger for the corporation that includes any stock ratified or validated in accordance with this section or with § 204 of this title;
-- src:746 | (6) Declare that shares of putative stock are shares of valid stock or require a corporation to issue and deliver shares of valid stock in place of any shares of putative stock;
-- src:747 | (7) Order that a meeting of holders of valid stock or putative stock be held and exercise the powers provided to the Court under § 227 of this title with respect to such a meeting;
-- src:748 | (8) Declare that a defective corporate act validated by the Court shall be effective as of the time of the defective corporate act or at such other time as the Court shall determine;
-- src:749 | (9) Declare that putative stock validated by the Court shall be deemed to be an identical share or fraction of a share of valid stock as of the time originally issued or purportedly issued or at such other time as the Court shall determine; and
-- src:750 | (10) Make such other orders regarding such matters as it deems proper under the circumstances.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(b) (src:740-750)
@export May the Court of Chancery make this order in connection with an action under section 205(b)?
GIVEN `the order` IS A `s 205(b) Order the Court may make` @desc Which order: a declaration that a ratification is not effective or only on conditions; validation with conditions; measures to remedy harm; an order to the Secretary of State to accept an instrument for filing; approval of a stock ledger; a declaration about putative shares; an order to hold a meeting; a declaration of effect as of a time; a declaration that putative stock is identical to valid stock; or another proper order?
      `an action under section 205 has been brought` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an action under section 205 been brought?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Court of Chancery make this order in my action` IF
    `s 205(b) the Court of Chancery may make the order in connection with the action` `the order` `an action under section 205 has been brought`

-- src:743 | (3) Require measures to remedy or avoid harm to any person substantially and adversely affected by a ratification pursuant to § 204 of this title or from any order of the Court pursuant to this section, excluding any harm that would have resulted if the defective corporate act had been valid when approved or effectuated;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(b)(3) (src:743)
@export Is this harm one for which the Court may require measures to remedy or avoid it (s 205(b)(3))?
GIVEN `I am substantially and adversely affected by a ratification under section 204 or by an order of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you substantially and adversely affected by a ratification under section 204 or by an order of the Court under section 205?
      `the harm would have resulted if the defective corporate act had been valid when approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the harm have resulted if the defective corporate act had been valid when approved or effectuated?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this harm harm the Court may require measures to remedy` IF
    `s 205(b)(3) the harm is harm the Court may require measures to remedy or avoid` `I am substantially and adversely affected by a ratification under section 204 or by an order of the Court` `the harm would have resulted if the defective corporate act had been valid when approved`

-- src:744 | (4) Order the Secretary of State to accept an instrument for filing with an effective time specified by the Court, which effective time may be prior or subsequent to the time of such order, provided that the filing date of such instrument shall be determined in accordance with § 103(c)(3) of this title;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(b)(4) (src:744)
@export What is the filing date of an instrument the Court orders the Secretary of State to accept for filing (s 205(b)(4))? It is the date determined under section 103(c)(3).
GIVEN `the filing date determined under section 103(c)(3)` IS A DATE @desc What is the filing date of the instrument determined under section 103(c)(3)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the filing date of an instrument the Court orders filed` IS
    `s 205(b)(4) the filing date of the instrument the Court orders accepted for filing` `the filing date determined under section 103(c)(3)`

-- src:751 | Service of the application under subsection (a) of this section upon the registered agent of the corporation shall be deemed to be service upon the corporation, and no other party need be joined in order for the Court of Chancery to adjudicate the matter. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(c) (src:751)
@export If I serve my application on the registered agent of the corporation, is the corporation deemed served (s 205(c))?
GIVEN `I served the application on the registered agent of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you serve the application on the registered agent of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as having served the corporation by serving its registered agent` IF
    `s 205(c) the corporation is deemed to have been served with the application` `I served the application on the registered agent of the corporation`

-- src:751 | Service of the application under subsection (a) of this section upon the registered agent of the corporation shall be deemed to be service upon the corporation, and no other party need be joined in order for the Court of Chancery to adjudicate the matter. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(c) (src:751)
@export Must another party be joined for the Court of Chancery to adjudicate my application (s 205(c))?
GIVEN `I have made an application under section 205(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made an application under section 205(a)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I join another party for the Court of Chancery to decide my application` IF
    `s 205(c) another party must be joined for the Court of Chancery to adjudicate the matter` `I have made an application under section 205(a)`

-- src:751 | In an action filed by the corporation, the Court may require notice of the action be provided to other persons specified by the Court and permit such other persons to intervene in the action.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(c) (src:751)
@export In an action the corporation filed, may the Court require notice to other persons and let them intervene (s 205(c))? Returns nothing if the corporation did not file the action.
GIVEN `the action was filed by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the action filed by the corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Court of Chancery require notice of the corporation's action to other persons` IS
    `s 205(c) the Court may require notice of the action to other persons and permit them to intervene` `the action was filed by the corporation`

-- src:752 | (d) In connection with the resolution of matters pursuant to subsections (a) and (b) of this section, the Court of Chancery may consider the following:
-- src:753 | (1) Whether the defective corporate act was originally approved or effectuated with the belief that the approval or effectuation was in compliance with the provisions of this title, the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of the corporation;
-- src:754 | (2) Whether the corporation and board of directors has treated the defective corporate act as a valid act or transaction and whether any person has acted in reliance on the public record that such defective corporate act was valid;
-- src:755 | (3) Whether any person will be or was harmed by the ratification or validation of the defective corporate act, excluding any harm that would have resulted if the defective corporate act had been valid when approved or effectuated;
-- src:756 | (4) Whether any person will be harmed by the failure to ratify or validate the defective corporate act; and
-- src:757 | (5) Any other factors or considerations the Court deems just and equitable.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(d) (src:752-757)
@export May the Court of Chancery consider this factor in resolving matters under section 205(a) and (b)?
GIVEN `the factor` IS A `s 205(d) Factor the Court may consider` @desc Which factor: whether the act was approved in the belief that it complied with the Law, the certificate or bylaws; whether the corporation and board treated it as valid and anyone relied on the public record; whether anyone will be or was harmed by ratification or validation; whether anyone will be harmed by failure to ratify or validate; or any other factor that is just and equitable?
      `the Court is resolving matters under section 205(a) and (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court resolving matters under subsections (a) and (b) of section 205?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Court of Chancery consider this factor` IF
    `s 205(d) the Court of Chancery may consider the factor` `the factor` `the Court is resolving matters under section 205(a) and (b)`

-- src:755 | (3) Whether any person will be or was harmed by the ratification or validation of the defective corporate act, excluding any harm that would have resulted if the defective corporate act had been valid when approved or effectuated;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(d)(3) (src:755)
@export Is the harm I will suffer or suffered from the ratification or validation harm the Court is to consider (s 205(d)(3))?
GIVEN `I will be or was harmed by the ratification or validation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will you be or were you harmed by the ratification or validation of the defective corporate act?
      `the harm would have resulted if the defective corporate act had been valid when approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the harm have resulted if the act had been valid when approved or effectuated?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the harm to me harm the Court considers` IF
    `s 205(d)(3) the harm is to be considered` `I will be or was harmed by the ratification or validation` `the harm would have resulted if the defective corporate act had been valid when approved`

-- src:758 | (e) The Court of Chancery is hereby vested with exclusive jurisdiction to hear and determine all actions brought under this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 205(e) (src:758)
@export Does the court have jurisdiction to hear and determine my action under section 205? Only the Court of Chancery does (s 205(e)).
GIVEN `my action is brought in the Court of Chancery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your action brought in the Court of Chancery?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Court of Chancery have jurisdiction over my action under section 205` IF
    `s 205(e) the court has jurisdiction to hear and determine the action brought under this section` `my action is brought in the Court of Chancery`

-- Subchapter VII (Meetings, Elections, Voting and Notice). Section 215(a) takes s 211(b), (c) and (e) out of a nonstock corporation: the questions
-- about them take the kind of corporation and return nothing if the provision does not apply to it.
§ `s 211 Meetings of stockholders`

§§ `s 211(a) Where the meeting is held, and taking part by remote communication`

-- src:767 | Meetings of stockholders may be held at such place, either within or without this State as may be designated by or in the manner provided in the certificate of incorporation or bylaws, or if not so designated, as determined by the board of directors. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(a)(1) (src:767)
@export Who decides where the meeting of stockholders is held (s 211(a)(1))?
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws designate the place, or provide the manner of designating it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws designate the place of the meeting, or provide the manner of designating it?
GIVETH A `s 211(a)(1) Who determines the place of a meeting`
DECIDE `Who decides where the stockholders' meeting is held` IS
    `s 211(a)(1) who determines the place of the meeting` `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws designate the place, or provide the manner of designating it`

-- src:767 | If, pursuant to this paragraph or the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws of the corporation, the board of directors is authorized to determine the place of a meeting of stockholders, the board of directors may, in its sole discretion, determine that the meeting shall not be held at any place, but may instead be held solely by means of remote communication as authorized by paragraph (a)(2) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(a)(1) (src:767)
@export May the board of directors decide that the meeting is held at no place but solely by remote communication (s 211(a)(1))?
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws designate the place, or provide the manner of designating it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws designate the place of the meeting, or provide the manner of designating it?
      `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws authorize the board of directors to determine the place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the certificate or bylaws authorize the board of directors to determine the place?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the board decide the meeting is held solely by remote communication` IF
    `s 211(a)(1) the board of directors may decide that the meeting is held solely by remote communication` `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws designate the place, or provide the manner of designating it` `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws authorize the board of directors to determine the place`

-- src:768 | (2) If authorized by the board of directors in its sole discretion, and subject to such guidelines and procedures as the board of directors may adopt, stockholders and proxyholders not physically present at a meeting of stockholders may, by means of remote communication:
-- src:769 | a. Participate in a meeting of stockholders; and
-- src:770 | b. Be deemed present in person and vote at a meeting of stockholders, whether such meeting is to be held at a designated place or solely by means of remote communication, provided that (i) the corporation shall implement reasonable measures to verify that each person deemed present and permitted to vote at the meeting by means of remote communication is a stockholder or proxyholder, (ii) the corporation shall implement reasonable measures to provide such stockholders and proxyholders a reasonable opportunity to participate in the meeting and to vote on matters submitted to the stockholders, including an opportunity to read or hear the proceedings of the meeting substantially concurrently with such proceedings, and (iii) if any stockholder or proxyholder votes or takes other action at the meeting by means of remote communication, a record of such vote or other action shall be maintained by the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(a)(2) (src:768-770)
@export May I, though not physically present, take part in the meeting of stockholders by remote communication (s 211(a)(2)a.)?
GIVEN `the board of directors has authorized it in its sole discretion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the board of directors authorized participation by remote communication?
      `I follow the guidelines and procedures the board of directors has adopted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you follow the guidelines and procedures the board has adopted?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I take part in the meeting by remote communication` IF
    `s 211(a)(2)a. the stockholder or proxyholder not physically present may participate in the meeting by remote communication` `the board of directors has authorized it in its sole discretion` `I follow the guidelines and procedures the board of directors has adopted`

-- src:768 | (2) If authorized by the board of directors in its sole discretion, and subject to such guidelines and procedures as the board of directors may adopt, stockholders and proxyholders not physically present at a meeting of stockholders may, by means of remote communication:
-- src:769 | a. Participate in a meeting of stockholders; and
-- src:770 | b. Be deemed present in person and vote at a meeting of stockholders, whether such meeting is to be held at a designated place or solely by means of remote communication, provided that (i) the corporation shall implement reasonable measures to verify that each person deemed present and permitted to vote at the meeting by means of remote communication is a stockholder or proxyholder, (ii) the corporation shall implement reasonable measures to provide such stockholders and proxyholders a reasonable opportunity to participate in the meeting and to vote on matters submitted to the stockholders, including an opportunity to read or hear the proceedings of the meeting substantially concurrently with such proceedings, and (iii) if any stockholder or proxyholder votes or takes other action at the meeting by means of remote communication, a record of such vote or other action shall be maintained by the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(a)(2) (src:768-770)
@export Am I deemed present in person, and may I vote at the meeting by remote communication (s 211(a)(2)b.)?
GIVEN `I may participate by remote communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May you participate by remote communication (see the question above)?
      `the corporation implements reasonable measures to verify that each person is a stockholder or proxyholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation implement reasonable measures to verify that each person deemed present and permitted to vote by remote communication is a stockholder or proxyholder?
      `the corporation implements reasonable measures to give a reasonable opportunity to participate and to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it implement reasonable measures to give them a reasonable opportunity to participate and to vote, including to read or hear the proceedings substantially concurrently?
      `a record of any vote or other action by remote communication is maintained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a record of any vote or other action taken by remote communication maintained by the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I deemed present in person and may I vote by remote communication` IF
    `s 211(a)(2)b. the person is deemed present in person and may vote by remote communication` `I may participate by remote communication` `the corporation implements reasonable measures to verify that each person is a stockholder or proxyholder` `the corporation implements reasonable measures to give a reasonable opportunity to participate and to vote` `a record of any vote or other action by remote communication is maintained`

§§ `s 211(b) The annual meeting`

-- src:771 | Unless directors are elected by written consent in lieu of an annual meeting as permitted by this subsection, an annual meeting of stockholders shall be held for the election of directors on a date and at a time designated by or in the manner provided in the bylaws. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(b) (src:771)
@export Must the corporation hold an annual meeting of stockholders for the election of directors (s 211(b))? Returns nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `directors are elected by written consent in lieu of an annual meeting as the subsection permits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the directors elected by written consent in lieu of an annual meeting, as section 211(b) permits?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation hold an annual meeting for the election of directors` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 211(b) of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 211(b) the corporation must hold an annual meeting of stockholders for the election of directors` `directors are elected by written consent in lieu of an annual meeting as the subsection permits`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:771 | Unless directors are elected by written consent in lieu of an annual meeting as permitted by this subsection, an annual meeting of stockholders shall be held for the election of directors on a date and at a time designated by or in the manner provided in the bylaws. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(b) (src:771)
@export Are the date and time of the annual meeting designated as section 211(b) requires, by or in the manner provided in the bylaws? Returns nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the date and time are designated by or in the manner provided in the bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the date and time designated by, or in the manner provided in, the bylaws?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the date and time of the annual meeting designated as required` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 211(b) of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 211(b) the date and time of the annual meeting are designated as the subsection requires` `the date and time are designated by or in the manner provided in the bylaws`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:771 | Stockholders may, unless the certificate of incorporation otherwise provides, act by written consent to elect directors; provided, however, that, if such consent is less than unanimous, such action by written consent may be in lieu of holding an annual meeting only if all of the directorships to which directors could be elected at an annual meeting held at the effective time of such action are vacant and are filled by such action. Any other proper business may be transacted at the annual meeting.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(b) (src:771)
@export May the stockholders act by written consent to elect directors (s 211(b))? Returns nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the certificate of incorporation otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation otherwise provide?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the stockholders act by written consent to elect directors` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 211(b) of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 211(b) the stockholders may act by written consent to elect directors` `the certificate of incorporation otherwise provides`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:771 | provided, however, that, if such consent is less than unanimous, such action by written consent may be in lieu of holding an annual meeting only if all of the directorships to which directors could be elected at an annual meeting held at the effective time of such action are vacant and are filled by such action. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(b) (src:771)
@export Does a written consent to elect directors take the place of the annual meeting (s 211(b))? Returns nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the consent is unanimous` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the consent unanimous?
      `all the directorships that could be filled at an annual meeting held at the effective time are vacant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If not, are all the directorships to which directors could be elected at an annual meeting held at the effective time of the action vacant?
      `they are filled by the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they filled by the action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a written consent take the place of the annual meeting` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 211(b) of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 211(b) the written consent takes the place of the annual meeting` `the consent is unanimous` `all the directorships that could be filled at an annual meeting held at the effective time are vacant` `they are filled by the action`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:771 | Any other proper business may be transacted at the annual meeting.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(b) (src:771)
@export May other proper business be transacted at the annual meeting (s 211(b))? Returns nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the business is proper` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the business proper?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May other proper business be transacted at the annual meeting` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 211(b) of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 211(b) the business may be transacted at the annual meeting` `the business is proper`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Situation: the annual meeting was not held when it should have been (or directors were not elected), so that a stockholder or director may ask the Court of Chancery to order it.
§§ `s 211(c) When the annual meeting is not held`

-- src:772 | A failure to hold the annual meeting at the designated time or to elect a sufficient number of directors to conduct the business of the corporation shall not affect otherwise valid corporate acts or work a forfeiture or dissolution of the corporation except as may be otherwise specifically provided in this chapter. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(c) (src:772)
@export Does a failure to hold the annual meeting, or to elect enough directors, affect otherwise valid corporate acts or work a forfeiture or dissolution (s 211(c))? Returns nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `this chapter specifically provides that it does` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Law specifically provide that the failure affects corporate acts or works a forfeiture or dissolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the failure to hold the annual meeting affect corporate acts or work a forfeiture` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 211(c) of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 211(c) the failure to hold the annual meeting or to elect enough directors affects otherwise valid corporate acts or works a forfeiture or dissolution` `this chapter specifically provides that it does`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:772 | If the annual meeting for election of directors is not held on the date designated therefor or action by written consent to elect directors in lieu of an annual meeting has not been taken, the directors shall cause the meeting to be held as soon as is convenient. If there be a failure to hold the annual meeting or to take action by written consent to elect directors in lieu of an annual meeting for a period of 30 days after the date designated for the annual meeting, or if no date has been designated, for a period of 13 months after the latest to occur of the organization of the corporation, its last annual meeting or the last action by written consent to elect directors in lieu of an annual meeting, the Court of Chancery may summarily order a meeting to be held upon the application of any stockholder or director. The shares of stock represented at such meeting, either in person or by proxy, and entitled to vote thereat, shall constitute a quorum for the purpose of such meeting, notwithstanding any provision of the certificate of incorporation or bylaws to the contrary. The Court of Chancery may issue such orders as may be appropriate, including, without limitation, orders designating the time and place of such meeting, the record date or dates for determination of stockholders entitled to notice of the meeting and to vote thereat, and the form of notice of such meeting.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(c) (src:772)
@export Must the directors cause the annual meeting to be held as soon as is convenient (s 211(c))? Returns nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the annual meeting was not held on the date designated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the annual meeting for the election of directors not held on the date designated?
      `no action by written consent to elect directors in lieu of an annual meeting has been taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has no action by written consent to elect directors in lieu of an annual meeting been taken?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the directors cause the annual meeting to be held` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 211(c) of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 211(c) the directors must cause the annual meeting to be held as soon as is convenient` `the annual meeting was not held on the date designated` `no action by written consent to elect directors in lieu of an annual meeting has been taken`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:772 | If there be a failure to hold the annual meeting or to take action by written consent to elect directors in lieu of an annual meeting for a period of 30 days after the date designated for the annual meeting, or if no date has been designated, for a period of 13 months after the latest to occur of the organization of the corporation, its last annual meeting or the last action by written consent to elect directors in lieu of an annual meeting, the Court of Chancery may summarily order a meeting to be held upon the application of any stockholder or director. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(c) (src:772)
@export May the Court of Chancery summarily order a meeting to be held on my application as a stockholder or director (s 211(c))? Returns nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `I am a stockholder or a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a stockholder or a director?
      `there has been no annual meeting and no written consent in lieu of one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has there been no annual meeting, and no action by written consent to elect directors in lieu of one, since the date designated (or since the events below)?
      `a date was designated for the annual meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a date designated for the annual meeting?
      `the day designated for the annual meeting` IS A DATE @desc What was that date? (ignored if none was designated)
      `the day the corporation was organized` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the corporation organized?
      `there has been an annual meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has there been an annual meeting?
      `the day of the last annual meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the last one? (ignored if none)
      `there has been a written consent to elect directors in lieu of an annual meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has there been an action by written consent to elect directors in lieu of an annual meeting?
      `the day of the last such consent` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the last one? (ignored if none)
      `the day of the application` IS A DATE @desc On what day would you apply?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask the Court of Chancery to order the annual meeting` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 211(c) of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 211(c) the Court of Chancery may summarily order a meeting to be held` `I am a stockholder or a director` `there has been no annual meeting and no written consent in lieu of one` designated `the day the corporation was organized` lastMeeting lastConsent `the day of the application`)
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        designated MEANS IF `a date was designated for the annual meeting` THEN JUST `the day designated for the annual meeting` ELSE NOTHING
        lastMeeting MEANS IF `there has been an annual meeting` THEN JUST `the day of the last annual meeting` ELSE NOTHING
        lastConsent MEANS IF `there has been a written consent to elect directors in lieu of an annual meeting` THEN JUST `the day of the last such consent` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:772 | The shares of stock represented at such meeting, either in person or by proxy, and entitled to vote thereat, shall constitute a quorum for the purpose of such meeting, notwithstanding any provision of the certificate of incorporation or bylaws to the contrary. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(c) (src:772)
@export Do the shares represented at the meeting the Court ordered constitute a quorum, despite the certificate or bylaws (s 211(c))? Returns nothing if no shares are represented, or if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the number of shares represented at the meeting in person or by proxy and entitled to vote there` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares are represented at the meeting, in person or by proxy, and entitled to vote there?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the shares represented at the court-ordered meeting form a quorum` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 211(c) of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN `s 211(c) the shares represented at the meeting the Court ordered constitute a quorum` `the number of shares represented at the meeting in person or by proxy and entitled to vote there`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:772 | The Court of Chancery may issue such orders as may be appropriate, including, without limitation, orders designating the time and place of such meeting, the record date or dates for determination of stockholders entitled to notice of the meeting and to vote thereat, and the form of notice of such meeting.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(c) (src:772)
@export May the Court of Chancery issue this order about the meeting it has ordered (s 211(c))? Returns nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the order` IS A `s 211(c) Order the Court may issue about the meeting it orders` @desc Which order: designating the time and place; designating the record date or dates; fixing the form of notice; or any other appropriate order?
      `the Court of Chancery has ordered a meeting under section 211(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court of Chancery ordered a meeting under section 211(c)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Court of Chancery issue this order about the meeting` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 211(c) of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 211(c) the Court of Chancery may issue the order` `the order` `the Court of Chancery has ordered a meeting under section 211(c)`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 211(d) and (e) Special meetings and ballots`

-- src:773 | (d) Special meetings of the stockholders may be called by the board of directors or by such person or persons as may be authorized by the certificate of incorporation or by the bylaws.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(d) (src:773)
@export May I call a special meeting of the stockholders (s 211(d))?
GIVEN `the call is made by the board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the call made by the board of directors?
      `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws authorize me to call a special meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws authorize you to call a special meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I call a special meeting of the stockholders` IF
    `s 211(d) the person may call a special meeting of the stockholders` `the call is made by the board of directors` `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws authorize me to call a special meeting`

-- src:774 | All elections of directors shall be by written ballot unless otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation; if authorized by the board of directors, such requirement of a written ballot shall be satisfied by a ballot submitted by electronic transmission, provided that any such electronic transmission must either set forth or be submitted with information from which it can be determined that the electronic transmission was authorized by the stockholder or proxy holder.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(e) (src:774)
@export Must the election of directors be by written ballot (s 211(e))? Returns nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation provide otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the election of directors be by written ballot` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 211(e) of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 211(e) the election of directors must be by written ballot` `the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:774 | if authorized by the board of directors, such requirement of a written ballot shall be satisfied by a ballot submitted by electronic transmission, provided that any such electronic transmission must either set forth or be submitted with information from which it can be determined that the electronic transmission was authorized by the stockholder or proxy holder.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 211(e) (src:774)
@export Does a ballot submitted by electronic transmission satisfy the requirement of a written ballot (s 211(e))? Returns nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the board of directors has authorized ballots by electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the board of directors authorized ballots by electronic transmission?
      `the electronic transmission sets forth, or is submitted with, information showing it was authorized by the stockholder or proxy holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the transmission set forth, or is it submitted with, information from which it can be determined that the stockholder or proxy holder authorized it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my ballot by electronic transmission satisfy the requirement of a written ballot` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 211(e) of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 211(e) a ballot submitted by electronic transmission satisfies the requirement of a written ballot` `the board of directors has authorized ballots by electronic transmission` `the electronic transmission sets forth, or is submitted with, information showing it was authorized by the stockholder or proxy holder`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 215(a) takes s 212(a) and (b), s 213 and s 214 out of a nonstock corporation (the member's questions are in the group for s 215);
-- s 212(c), (d) and (e) apply to it. The questions about the provisions taken out return nothing if the provision does not apply to my kind of corporation.
§ `s 212, s 213 and s 214: votes, proxies, record dates and cumulative voting`

§§ `s 212(a) How many votes I have`

-- src:778 | (a) Unless otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation and subject to § 213 of this title, each stockholder shall be entitled to 1 vote for each share of capital stock held by such stockholder. If the certificate of incorporation provides for more or less than 1 vote for any share, on any matter, every reference in this chapter to a majority or other proportion of stock, voting stock or shares shall refer to such majority or other proportion of the votes of such stock, voting stock or shares.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 212(a) (src:778)
@export How many votes does each share of capital stock carry on the matter (s 212(a))? One, unless the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise. Returns nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the certificate of incorporation provides for a number of votes other than 1 for the share, on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation provide for more or fewer than 1 vote for a share, on this matter?
      `the number of votes the certificate of incorporation gives the share, on the matter` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes does it give each share on this matter? (ignored if it provides none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many votes does each of my shares carry on the matter` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 212(a) of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 212(a) the number of votes each share carries on the matter` `the certificate of incorporation provides for a number of votes other than 1 for the share, on the matter` `the number of votes the certificate of incorporation gives the share, on the matter`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:778 | (a) Unless otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation and subject to § 213 of this title, each stockholder shall be entitled to 1 vote for each share of capital stock held by such stockholder. If the certificate of incorporation provides for more or less than 1 vote for any share, on any matter, every reference in this chapter to a majority or other proportion of stock, voting stock or shares shall refer to such majority or other proportion of the votes of such stock, voting stock or shares.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 212(a) (src:778)
@export How many votes am I entitled to cast on the matter (s 212(a))? Counted in votes, because every reference in the Law to a proportion of stock refers to the votes of that stock. Returns nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `I am entitled to vote at the meeting under section 213` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a stockholder entitled to vote at the meeting under section 213 (a stockholder of record on the record date)?
      `the number of shares of capital stock I hold` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of capital stock do you hold?
      `the certificate of incorporation provides for a number of votes other than 1 for the share, on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation provide for more or fewer than 1 vote for a share, on this matter?
      `the number of votes the certificate of incorporation gives the share, on the matter` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes does it give each share on this matter? (ignored if it provides none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many votes may I cast` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 212(a) of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 212(a) the number of votes the stockholder is entitled to cast` `I am entitled to vote at the meeting under section 213` `the number of shares of capital stock I hold` (`s 212(a) the number of votes each share carries on the matter` `the certificate of incorporation provides for a number of votes other than 1 for the share, on the matter` `the number of votes the certificate of incorporation gives the share, on the matter`))
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 212(b) to (e) Proxies`

-- src:779 | Each stockholder entitled to vote at a meeting of stockholders or to express consent or dissent to corporate action in writing without a meeting may authorize another person or persons to act for such stockholder by proxy, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 212(b) (src:779)
@export May I authorize another person or persons to act for me by proxy (s 212(b))? Returns nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `I am entitled to vote at a meeting of stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to vote at a meeting of stockholders?
      `I am entitled to express consent or dissent to corporate action in writing without a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to express consent or dissent to corporate action in writing without a meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I authorize another person to act for me by proxy` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 212(b) of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 212(b) the stockholder may authorize another person or persons to act for the stockholder by proxy` `I am entitled to vote at a meeting of stockholders` `I am entitled to express consent or dissent to corporate action in writing without a meeting`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:779 | but no such proxy shall be voted or acted upon after 3 years from its date, unless the proxy provides for a longer period.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 212(b) (src:779)
@export Can the proxy still be voted or acted upon, or has the 3-year limit run (s 212(b))? Returns nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the date of the proxy` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the proxy?
      `the proxy provides for a longer period than 3 years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the proxy provide for a longer period than 3 years?
      `the longer period has a last day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does the longer period have a definite last day?
      `the last day of that longer period` IS A DATE @desc What is it? (ignored if none)
      `the day the proxy would be voted or acted upon` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the proxy be voted or acted upon?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my proxy still be voted or acted upon` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 212(b) of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 212(b) the three-year limit does not stop the proxy being voted or acted upon` `the date of the proxy` `the proxy provides for a longer period than 3 years` lastDay `the day the proxy would be voted or acted upon`)
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        lastDay MEANS IF `the longer period has a last day` THEN JUST `the last day of that longer period` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:780 | (c) Without limiting the manner in which a stockholder may authorize another person or persons to act for such stockholder as proxy pursuant to subsection (b) of this section, the following shall constitute a valid means by which a stockholder may grant such authority:
-- src:781 | (1) A stockholder, or such stockholder’s authorized officer, director, employee or agent, may execute a document authorizing another person or persons to act for such stockholder as proxy.
-- src:782 | (2) A stockholder may authorize another person or persons to act for such stockholder as proxy by transmitting or authorizing the transmission of an electronic transmission to the person who will be the holder of the proxy or to a proxy solicitation firm, proxy support service organization or like agent duly authorized by the person who will be the holder of the proxy to receive such transmission, provided that any such transmission must either set forth or be submitted with information from which it can be determined that the transmission was authorized by the stockholder. If it is determined that such transmissions are valid, the inspectors or, if there are no inspectors, such other persons making that determination shall specify the information upon which they relied.
-- src:783 | (3) The authorization of a person to act as a proxy may be documented, signed and delivered in accordance with § 116 of this title, provided that such authorization shall set forth, or be delivered with information enabling the corporation to determine, the identity of the stockholder granting such authorization.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 212(c) (src:780-783)
@export Is this a valid means by which I may authorize another person to act for me as proxy (s 212(c))? The list is not exclusive, so a means that does not qualify returns nothing, not no.
GIVEN `the way` IS A `s 212(c) Way of authorizing a proxy` @desc How do you authorize the proxy: by a document executed by you or your authorized officer, director, employee or agent; by electronic transmission to the proxy holder or an authorized proxy solicitation firm or like agent; or by an authorization documented, signed and delivered in accordance with section 116?
      `the document was executed by me or by my authorized officer, director, employee or agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the document executed by you or by your authorized officer, director, employee or agent?
      `the electronic transmission was sent to the proxy holder or to an agent duly authorized to receive it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the electronic transmission sent to the person who will hold the proxy, or to a proxy solicitation firm, proxy support service organization or like agent duly authorized by that person to receive it?
      `the transmission sets forth, or is submitted with, information showing that I authorized it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the transmission set forth, or is it submitted with, information from which it can be determined that you authorized it?
      `the authorization was documented, signed and delivered in accordance with section 116` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the authorization documented, signed and delivered in accordance with section 116?
      `the authorization sets forth, or is delivered with information enabling the corporation to determine, my identity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the authorization set forth, or is it delivered with information enabling the corporation to determine, your identity as the stockholder?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this a valid way for me to authorize a proxy` IS
    `s 212(c) the way of authorizing the proxy is a valid means` `the way` facts
    WHERE
        facts MEANS `s 212(c) Facts about the authorization` WITH
            `the document was executed by the stockholder or by the stockholder's authorized officer, director, employee or agent` IS `the document was executed by me or by my authorized officer, director, employee or agent`
            `the electronic transmission was sent to the person who will hold the proxy or to an agent duly authorized by that person to receive it` IS `the electronic transmission was sent to the proxy holder or to an agent duly authorized to receive it`
            `the transmission sets forth, or is submitted with, information from which it can be determined that the stockholder authorized it` IS `the transmission sets forth, or is submitted with, information showing that I authorized it`
            `the authorization was documented, signed and delivered in accordance with s 116` IS `the authorization was documented, signed and delivered in accordance with section 116`
            `the authorization sets forth, or is delivered with information enabling the corporation to determine, the identity of the stockholder` IS `the authorization sets forth, or is delivered with information enabling the corporation to determine, my identity`

-- src:782 | If it is determined that such transmissions are valid, the inspectors or, if there are no inspectors, such other persons making that determination shall specify the information upon which they relied.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 212(c)(2) (src:782)
@export If it is determined that electronic proxy transmissions are valid, must the inspectors (or the other persons making the determination) specify the information they relied on (s 212(c)(2))?
GIVEN `it is determined that the transmissions are valid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been determined that the transmissions are valid?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the inspectors say what information they relied on` IF
    `s 212(c)(2) the inspectors or the other persons making the determination must specify the information upon which they relied` `it is determined that the transmissions are valid`

-- src:784 | (d) Any copy, facsimile telecommunication or other reliable reproduction of the document (including any electronic transmission) created pursuant to subsection (c) of this section may be substituted or used in lieu of the original document for any and all purposes for which the original document could be used, provided that such copy, facsimile telecommunication or other reproduction shall be a complete reproduction of the entire original document.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 212(d) (src:784)
@export May a copy, facsimile or other reproduction of the proxy document be used in place of the original (s 212(d))?
GIVEN `it is a copy, facsimile telecommunication or other reliable reproduction of a document created under section 212(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a copy, facsimile telecommunication or other reliable reproduction (including an electronic transmission) of a document created under section 212(c)?
      `it is a complete reproduction of the entire original document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a complete reproduction of the entire original document?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a copy of the proxy document be used in place of the original` IF
    `s 212(d) the reproduction may be substituted or used in lieu of the original for any purpose for which the original could be used` `it is a copy, facsimile telecommunication or other reliable reproduction of a document created under section 212(c)` `it is a complete reproduction of the entire original document`

-- src:785 | (e) A duly executed proxy shall be irrevocable if it states that it is irrevocable and if, and only as long as, it is coupled with an interest sufficient in law to support an irrevocable power. A proxy may be made irrevocable regardless of whether the interest with which it is coupled is an interest in the stock itself or an interest in the corporation generally.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 212(e) (src:785)
@export Is the proxy irrevocable (s 212(e))?
GIVEN `the proxy is duly executed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proxy duly executed?
      `the proxy states that it is irrevocable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that it is irrevocable?
      `the interest` IS A `s 212(e) Interest coupled with a proxy` @desc Is it coupled with an interest in the stock itself, an interest in the corporation generally, or no interest?
      `the interest is sufficient in law to support an irrevocable power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that interest sufficient in law to support an irrevocable power?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my proxy irrevocable` IF
    `s 212(e) the proxy is irrevocable` `the proxy is duly executed` `the proxy states that it is irrevocable` `the interest` `the interest is sufficient in law to support an irrevocable power`

§§ `s 213 The record date`

-- src:789 | In order that the corporation may determine the stockholders entitled to notice of any meeting of stockholders or any adjournment thereof, the board of directors may fix a record date, which record date shall not precede the date upon which the resolution fixing the record date is adopted by the board of directors, and which record date shall not be more than 60 nor less than 10 days before the date of such meeting. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 213(a) (src:789)
@export May the board of directors fix this day as the record date for determining who is entitled to notice of the meeting (s 213(a))? Returns nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the day proposed as the record date` IS A DATE @desc What day is proposed as the record date?
      `the day the board adopts the resolution fixing the record date` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the board adopt the resolution fixing it?
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the board fix this day as the record date for the meeting` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 213 of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 213(a) the board of directors may fix the day as the record date for the meeting` `the day proposed as the record date` `the day the board adopts the resolution fixing the record date` `the day of the meeting`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:789 | If the board of directors so fixes a date, such date shall also be the record date for determining the stockholders entitled to vote at such meeting unless the board of directors determines, at the time it fixes such record date, that a later date on or before the date of the meeting shall be the date for making such determination. If no record date is fixed by the board of directors, the record date for determining stockholders entitled to notice of and to vote at a meeting of stockholders shall be at the close of business on the day next preceding the day on which notice is given, or, if notice is waived, at the close of business on the day next preceding the day on which the meeting is held. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 213(a) (src:789)
@export What is the record date for determining the stockholders entitled to notice of the meeting (s 213(a))? Returns nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the board fixed a record date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the board of directors fix a record date?
      `the record date the board fixed` IS A DATE @desc What is it? (ignored if it fixed none)
      `the day notice is given` IS A DATE @desc On what day is notice given?
      `notice is waived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is notice waived?
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `What is the record date for notice of the meeting` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 213 of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 213(a) the record date for the stockholders entitled to notice of the meeting` fixed `the day notice is given` `notice is waived` `the day of the meeting`)
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        fixed MEANS IF `the board fixed a record date` THEN JUST `the record date the board fixed` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:789 | If the board of directors so fixes a date, such date shall also be the record date for determining the stockholders entitled to vote at such meeting unless the board of directors determines, at the time it fixes such record date, that a later date on or before the date of the meeting shall be the date for making such determination. If no record date is fixed by the board of directors, the record date for determining stockholders entitled to notice of and to vote at a meeting of stockholders shall be at the close of business on the day next preceding the day on which notice is given, or, if notice is waived, at the close of business on the day next preceding the day on which the meeting is held. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 213(a) (src:789)
@export What is the record date for determining the stockholders entitled to vote at the meeting (s 213(a))? Returns nothing if the board's later date is not later than the one it fixed or falls after the meeting, or if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the board fixed a record date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the board of directors fix a record date?
      `the record date the board fixed` IS A DATE @desc What is it? (ignored if it fixed none)
      `the board determined a later date for voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When it fixed that date, did the board determine that a later date on or before the meeting should be the date for determining who votes?
      `the later date the board determined` IS A DATE @desc What is the later date? (ignored if none)
      `the day notice is given` IS A DATE @desc On what day is notice given?
      `notice is waived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is notice waived?
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `What is the record date for voting at the meeting` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 213 of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN `s 213(a) the record date for the stockholders entitled to vote at the meeting` fixed later `the day notice is given` `notice is waived` `the day of the meeting`
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        fixed MEANS IF `the board fixed a record date` THEN JUST `the record date the board fixed` ELSE NOTHING
        later MEANS IF `the board determined a later date for voting` THEN JUST `the later date the board determined` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:789 | A determination of stockholders of record entitled to notice of or to vote at a meeting of stockholders shall apply to any adjournment of the meeting; provided, however, that the board of directors may fix a new record date for determination of stockholders entitled to vote at the adjourned meeting, and in such case shall also fix as the record date for stockholders entitled to notice of such adjourned meeting the same or an earlier date as that fixed for determination of stockholders entitled to vote in accordance with the foregoing provisions of this subsection (a) at the adjourned meeting.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 213(a) (src:789)
@export Does the earlier determination of stockholders of record apply to the adjourned meeting (s 213(a))? Returns nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the board fixes a new record date for determining the stockholders entitled to vote at the adjourned meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the board fix a new record date for determining who may vote at the adjourned meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the earlier record date apply to the adjourned meeting` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 213 of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 213(a) the earlier determination of stockholders of record applies to the adjourned meeting` `the board fixes a new record date for determining the stockholders entitled to vote at the adjourned meeting`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:789 | A determination of stockholders of record entitled to notice of or to vote at a meeting of stockholders shall apply to any adjournment of the meeting; provided, however, that the board of directors may fix a new record date for determination of stockholders entitled to vote at the adjourned meeting, and in such case shall also fix as the record date for stockholders entitled to notice of such adjourned meeting the same or an earlier date as that fixed for determination of stockholders entitled to vote in accordance with the foregoing provisions of this subsection (a) at the adjourned meeting.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 213(a) (src:789)
@export Is the record date fixed for notice of the adjourned meeting the same as or earlier than the one fixed for voting at it (s 213(a))? Returns nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the record date fixed for notice of the adjourned meeting` IS A DATE @desc What record date is fixed for notice of the adjourned meeting?
      `the record date fixed for voting at the adjourned meeting` IS A DATE @desc What record date is fixed for determining who may vote at it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the record date for notice of the adjourned meeting permitted` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 213 of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 213(a) the record date for notice of the adjourned meeting is the same as or earlier than the record date for voting` `the record date fixed for notice of the adjourned meeting` `the record date fixed for voting at the adjourned meeting`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:789 | In order that the corporation may determine the stockholders entitled to notice of any meeting of stockholders or any adjournment thereof, the board of directors may fix a record date, which record date shall not precede the date upon which the resolution fixing the record date is adopted by the board of directors, and which record date shall not be more than 60 nor less than 10 days before the date of such meeting. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 213(a) (src:789)
@export Was I a stockholder of record at the close of business on the record date (s 213(a)), so that I am entitled to notice and to vote? Returns nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the day I became a stockholder of record` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you become a stockholder of record?
      `I have ceased to be a stockholder of record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you ceased to be a stockholder of record?
      `the day I ceased to be a stockholder of record` IS A DATE @desc On what day? (ignored if you have not)
      `the record date` IS A DATE @desc What is the record date?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I a stockholder of record at the close of business on the record date` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 213 of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 213 the person was a stockholder of record at the close of business on the record date` `the day I became a stockholder of record` ceased `the record date`)
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        ceased MEANS IF `I have ceased to be a stockholder of record` THEN JUST `the day I ceased to be a stockholder of record` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:790 | In order that the corporation may determine the stockholders entitled to consent to corporate action without a meeting in accordance with § 228 of this title, the board of directors may fix a record date, which record date shall not precede the date upon which the resolution fixing the record date is adopted by the board of directors, and which date shall not be more than 10 days after the date upon which the resolution fixing the record date is adopted by the board of directors. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 213(b) (src:790)
@export May the board of directors fix this day as the record date for stockholders to consent to corporate action without a meeting (s 213(b))? Returns nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the day proposed as the record date` IS A DATE @desc What day is proposed as the record date?
      `the day the board adopts the resolution fixing the record date` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the board adopt the resolution fixing it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the board fix this day as the record date for action by written consent` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 213 of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 213(b) the board of directors may fix the day as the record date for consent without a meeting` `the day proposed as the record date` `the day the board adopts the resolution fixing the record date`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:790 | If no record date has been fixed by the board of directors, the record date for determining stockholders entitled to consent to corporate action without a meeting, when no prior action by the board of directors is required by this chapter, shall be the first date on which a signed consent setting forth the action taken or proposed to be taken is delivered to the corporation in accordance with § 228(d) of this title. If no record date has been fixed by the board of directors and prior action by the board of directors is required by this chapter, the record date for determining stockholders entitled to consent to corporate action in writing without a meeting shall be at the close of business on the day on which the board of directors adopts the resolution taking such prior action.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 213(b) (src:790)
@export What is the record date for stockholders entitled to consent to corporate action without a meeting, where the board has fixed none (s 213(b))? Returns nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation, or if the date it depends on has not yet occurred.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the board fixed a record date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the board of directors fix a record date?
      `the record date the board fixed` IS A DATE @desc What is it? (ignored if it fixed none)
      `prior action by the board of directors is required by the Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Law require prior action by the board of directors for the action to be taken?
      `a signed consent has been delivered to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a signed consent setting forth the action been delivered to the corporation in accordance with section 228(d)?
      `the first day a signed consent was delivered` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the first one delivered? (ignored if none)
      `the board has adopted the resolution taking the prior action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the board adopted the resolution taking the prior action?
      `the day the board adopted the resolution taking the prior action` IS A DATE @desc On what day? (ignored if it has not)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `What is the record date for action by written consent` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 213 of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN `s 213(b) the record date for consent without a meeting` fixed `prior action by the board of directors is required by the Law` firstConsent boardDay
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        fixed MEANS IF `the board fixed a record date` THEN JUST `the record date the board fixed` ELSE NOTHING
        firstConsent MEANS IF `a signed consent has been delivered to the corporation` THEN JUST `the first day a signed consent was delivered` ELSE NOTHING
        boardDay MEANS IF `the board has adopted the resolution taking the prior action` THEN JUST `the day the board adopted the resolution taking the prior action` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:791 | In order that the corporation may determine the stockholders entitled to receive payment of any dividend or other distribution or allotment of any rights or the stockholders entitled to exercise any rights in respect of any change, conversion or exchange of stock, or for the purpose of any other lawful action, the board of directors may fix a record date, which record date shall not precede the date upon which the resolution fixing the record date is adopted, and which record date shall be not more than 60 days prior to such action. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 213(c) (src:791)
@export May the board of directors fix this day as the record date for a dividend, distribution, rights, a change, conversion or exchange of stock, or any other lawful action (s 213(c))? Returns nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the day proposed as the record date` IS A DATE @desc What day is proposed as the record date?
      `the day the board adopts the resolution fixing the record date` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the board adopt the resolution fixing it?
      `the day of the action` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the board fix this day as the record date for another purpose` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 213 of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 213(c) the board of directors may fix the day as the record date for the other purpose` `the day proposed as the record date` `the day the board adopts the resolution fixing the record date` `the day of the action`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:791 | If no record date is fixed, the record date for determining stockholders for any such purpose shall be at the close of business on the day on which the board of directors adopts the resolution relating thereto.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 213(c) (src:791)
@export What is the record date for a dividend, distribution or any other lawful action, where the board has fixed none (s 213(c))? Returns nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the board fixed a record date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the board of directors fix a record date?
      `the record date the board fixed` IS A DATE @desc What is it? (ignored if it fixed none)
      `the day the board adopts the resolution relating to the action` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the board adopt the resolution relating to the action?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `What is the record date for another purpose` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 213 of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 213(c) the record date for the other purpose` fixed `the day the board adopts the resolution relating to the action`)
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        fixed MEANS IF `the board fixed a record date` THEN JUST `the record date the board fixed` ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 214 Cumulative voting`

-- src:795 | The certificate of incorporation of any corporation may provide that at all elections of directors of the corporation, or at elections held under specified circumstances, each holder of stock or of any class or classes or of a series or series thereof shall be entitled to as many votes as shall equal the number of votes which (except for such provision as to cumulative voting) such holder would be entitled to cast for the election of directors with respect to such holder’s shares of stock multiplied by the number of directors to be elected by such holder, and that such holder may cast all of such votes for a single director or may distribute them among the number to be voted for, or for any 2 or more of them as such holder may see fit.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 214 (src:795)
@export How many votes may I cast in the election of directors if the certificate of incorporation provides for cumulative voting (s 214)? Returns nothing if it does not, or if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the certificate of incorporation provides for cumulative voting at this election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation provide for cumulative voting at this election?
      `my stock is of a class or series the provision covers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your stock of a class or series the provision covers?
      `the votes I would be entitled to cast for the election of directors apart from cumulative voting` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes would you be entitled to cast for the election of directors with respect to your shares, apart from cumulative voting?
      `the number of directors to be elected by me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors are to be elected by you (by your class or series)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many votes may I cast in the election of directors under cumulative voting` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 214 of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN `s 214 the number of votes the holder is entitled to cast in the election of directors` `the certificate of incorporation provides for cumulative voting at this election` `my stock is of a class or series the provision covers` `the votes I would be entitled to cast for the election of directors apart from cumulative voting` `the number of directors to be elected by me`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:795 | The certificate of incorporation of any corporation may provide that at all elections of directors of the corporation, or at elections held under specified circumstances, each holder of stock or of any class or classes or of a series or series thereof shall be entitled to as many votes as shall equal the number of votes which (except for such provision as to cumulative voting) such holder would be entitled to cast for the election of directors with respect to such holder’s shares of stock multiplied by the number of directors to be elected by such holder, and that such holder may cast all of such votes for a single director or may distribute them among the number to be voted for, or for any 2 or more of them as such holder may see fit.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 214 (src:795)
@export May I cast all my votes for a single director or distribute them among the directors to be voted for, under cumulative voting (s 214)? Returns nothing if the certificate does not provide for it, or if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the certificate of incorporation provides for cumulative voting at this election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation provide for cumulative voting at this election?
      `my stock is of a class or series the provision covers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your stock of a class or series the provision covers?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I cast all my votes for a single director` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 214 of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN `s 214 the holder may cast all the votes for a single director or distribute them among the directors to be voted for` `the certificate of incorporation provides for cumulative voting at this election` `my stock is of a class or series the provision covers`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 215(a) says ss 211 to 214 and 216 do not apply to a nonstock corporation (with exceptions); s 215(b) to (f) are the member's rules.
-- The questions for s 216 take the kind of corporation and return nothing if s 216 does not apply to it; the questions for s 215 return nothing for a stock corporation.
§ `s 215 and s 216: members of a nonstock corporation; quorum and required vote`

§§ `s 215(a) Does the provision apply to my corporation, and how is it read?`

-- src:799 | Sections 211 through 214 and 216 of this title shall not apply to nonstock corporations, except that § 211(a) and (d) of this title and § 212(c), (d), and (e) of this title shall apply to such corporations, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(a) (src:799)
@export Does this provision of sections 211 to 214 and 216 apply to my kind of corporation (s 215(a))?
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `s 215(a) Provision of ss 211 to 214 and 216` @desc Which provision: section 211(a), (b), (c), (d) or (e); 212(a), (b), (c), (d) or (e); 213; 214; or 216?
      `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this provision of sections 211 to 214 and 216 apply to my corporation` IF
    `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `the provision` `the kind of corporation`

-- src:799 | and, when so applied, all references therein to stockholders and to the board of directors shall be deemed to refer to the members and the governing body of a nonstock corporation, respectively; and all references to stock, capital stock, or shares thereof shall be deemed to refer to memberships of a nonprofit nonstock corporation and to membership interests of any other nonstock corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(a) (src:799)
@export How is a reference to stock, capital stock or shares read in my kind of corporation (s 215(a))?
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
GIVETH A `s 215(a) What a reference to stock is read as`
DECIDE `How is a reference to stock read in my corporation` IS
    `s 215(a) a reference to stock, capital stock or shares is read as` `the kind of corporation`

-- src:799 | and, when so applied, all references therein to stockholders and to the board of directors shall be deemed to refer to the members and the governing body of a nonstock corporation, respectively; and all references to stock, capital stock, or shares thereof shall be deemed to refer to memberships of a nonprofit nonstock corporation and to membership interests of any other nonstock corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(a) (src:799)
@export How is a reference to stockholders read in my kind of corporation (s 215(a))?
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
GIVETH A Actor
DECIDE `How is a reference to stockholders read in my corporation` IS
    `s 215(a) a reference to stockholders is read as` `the kind of corporation`

-- src:799 | and, when so applied, all references therein to stockholders and to the board of directors shall be deemed to refer to the members and the governing body of a nonstock corporation, respectively; and all references to stock, capital stock, or shares thereof shall be deemed to refer to memberships of a nonprofit nonstock corporation and to membership interests of any other nonstock corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(a) (src:799)
@export How is a reference to the board of directors read in my kind of corporation (s 215(a))?
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
GIVETH A `s 215(a) What a reference to the board of directors is read as`
DECIDE `How is a reference to the board of directors read in my corporation` IS
    `s 215(a) a reference to the board of directors is read as` `the kind of corporation`

-- Situation: the corporation is a nonstock corporation and I am a member.
§§ `s 215(b) to (f) A member's votes, quorum and election`

-- src:800 | (b) Unless otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws of a nonstock corporation, and subject to subsection (f) of this section, each member shall be entitled at every meeting of members to 1 vote on each matter submitted to a vote of members. A member may exercise such voting rights in person or by proxy, but no proxy shall be voted on after 3 years from its date, unless the proxy provides for a longer period.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(b) (src:800)
@export How many votes is a member of a nonstock corporation entitled to on each matter (s 215(b))? One, unless the certificate or bylaws provide otherwise. Returns nothing for a stock corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws provide for a number of votes other than 1 for the member on a matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws provide for a number of votes other than 1 for a member on a matter?
      `the number of votes they give the member on the matter` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes do they give a member on the matter? (ignored if they provide none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many votes is a member entitled to on each matter` IS
    IF `the kind is a nonstock corporation` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 215(b) the number of votes the member is entitled to on each matter` `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws provide for a number of votes other than 1 for the member on a matter` `the number of votes they give the member on the matter`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:800 | (b) Unless otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws of a nonstock corporation, and subject to subsection (f) of this section, each member shall be entitled at every meeting of members to 1 vote on each matter submitted to a vote of members. A member may exercise such voting rights in person or by proxy, but no proxy shall be voted on after 3 years from its date, unless the proxy provides for a longer period.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(b) (src:800)
@export Can a member's proxy still be voted on, or has the 3-year limit run (s 215(b))? Returns nothing for a stock corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the date of the proxy` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the proxy?
      `the proxy provides for a longer period than 3 years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the proxy provide for a longer period than 3 years?
      `the longer period has a last day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does the longer period have a definite last day?
      `the last day of that longer period` IS A DATE @desc What is it? (ignored if none)
      `the day the proxy would be voted on` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the proxy be voted on?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the member's proxy still be voted on` IS
    IF `the kind is a nonstock corporation` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 215(b) the three-year limit does not stop the member's proxy being voted on` `the date of the proxy` `the proxy provides for a longer period than 3 years` lastDay `the day the proxy would be voted on`)
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        lastDay MEANS IF `the longer period has a last day` THEN JUST `the last day of that longer period` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:801 | Unless otherwise provided in this chapter, the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of a nonstock corporation may specify the number of members having voting power who shall be present or represented by proxy at any meeting in order to constitute a quorum for, and the votes that shall be necessary for, the transaction of any business. In the absence of such specification in the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of a nonstock corporation:
-- src:802 | (1) One-third of the members of such corporation shall constitute a quorum at a meeting of such members;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(c) (src:801); § 215(c)(1) (src:802)
@export Is a quorum of members present at the meeting (s 215(c)(1))? One-third of the members unless the certificate or bylaws specify otherwise. Returns nothing for a stock corporation, or if the counts cannot be a vote.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws specify a quorum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws specify the number of members that constitutes a quorum?
      `the number of members they specify` IS A NUMBER @desc How many? (ignored if they specify none)
      `the number of members entitled to vote at the meeting` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members are entitled to vote at the meeting?
      `the number of members present in person or represented by proxy` IS A NUMBER @desc How many are present in person or represented by proxy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a quorum of members present` IS
    IF `the kind is a nonstock corporation` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN `s 215(c)(1) a quorum of members is present` specified `the number of members entitled to vote at the meeting` `the number of members present in person or represented by proxy`
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        specified MEANS IF `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws specify a quorum` THEN JUST `the number of members they specify` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:803 | (2) In all matters other than the election of the governing body of such corporation, the affirmative vote of a majority of such members present in person or represented by proxy at the meeting and entitled to vote on the subject matter shall be the act of the members, unless the vote of a greater number is required by this chapter;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(c)(2) (src:803)
@export Is a matter other than the election of the governing body the act of the members (s 215(c)(2))? A majority of the members present and entitled to vote on it, unless a greater vote is required. Returns nothing for a stock corporation, or if the counts cannot be a vote.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `a vote other than a majority of the votes present applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Law require, or do the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws specify, a vote other than the default (a majority of the votes present and entitled to vote on the subject matter)? Give the one that applies: the Law's, if it requires one.
      `the numerator of the fraction required` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the fraction of the votes required: the numerator? (for two-thirds, 2; ignored if the default applies)
      `the denominator of the fraction required` IS A NUMBER @desc The denominator? (for two-thirds, 3; ignored if the default applies)
      `the fraction must be exceeded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Must the fraction be exceeded ("a majority"), rather than merely reached ("at least")? (ignored if the default applies)
      `the fraction is of the votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the fraction of the outstanding votes entitled to vote, rather than of the votes present? (ignored if the default applies)
      `the number of votes in favor` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes are in favor?
      `the number of votes of the members entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes do the members entitled to vote hold in all?
      `the number of votes present in person or represented by proxy and entitled to vote on the matter` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes are present in person or by proxy and entitled to vote on the matter?
      `the number of votes cast` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the matter the act of the members` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the kind is a nonstock corporation` `the kind of corporation`)) THEN NOTHING
        IF invalidFraction THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE `s 215(c)(2) the matter other than the election of the governing body is the act of the members` appliedVote NOTHING `the number of votes in favor` `the number of votes of the members entitled to vote` `the number of votes present in person or represented by proxy and entitled to vote on the matter` `the number of votes cast`
    WHERE
        appliedVote MEANS IF `a vote other than a majority of the votes present applies` THEN JUST requirement ELSE NOTHING
        requirement MEANS `Vote requirement` WITH
            `counted against` IS base
            proportion IS fraction
            `must be exceeded` IS `the fraction must be exceeded`
        base MEANS IF `the fraction is of the votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote` THEN `the outstanding stock entitled to vote` ELSE `the shares present in person or represented by proxy and entitled to vote`
        fraction MEANS IF `the denominator of the fraction required` GREATER THAN 0 THEN `the numerator of the fraction required` DIVIDED BY `the denominator of the fraction required` ELSE 0
        invalidFraction MEANS `a vote other than a majority of the votes present applies` AND `the denominator of the fraction required` AT MOST 0

-- src:804 | (3) Members of the governing body shall be elected by a plurality of the votes of the members of the corporation present in person or represented by proxy at the meeting and entitled to vote thereon; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(c)(3) (src:804)
@export Am I elected to the governing body by a plurality of the votes of the members present and entitled to vote (s 215(c)(3))? Returns nothing for a stock corporation, or if there is a tie for the last place.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the votes for me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast for you?
      `the votes for each other candidate` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast for each other candidate?
      `the number of members of the governing body to be elected` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members of the governing body are to be elected?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I elected to the governing body by a plurality of the votes` IS
    IF `the kind is a nonstock corporation` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN `s 215(c)(3) the candidate is elected to the governing body by a plurality of the votes` `the votes for me` `the votes for each other candidate` `the number of members of the governing body to be elected`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:805 | (4) Where a separate vote by a class or group or classes or groups is required, a majority of the members of such class or group or classes or groups, present in person or represented by proxy, shall constitute a quorum entitled to take action with respect to that vote on that matter and, in all matters other than the election of members of the governing body, the affirmative vote of the majority of the members of such class or group or classes or groups present in person or represented by proxy at the meeting shall be the act of such class or group or classes or groups.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(c)(4) (src:805)
@export Where a separate vote by a class or group of members is required, is a majority of its members present, so that it has a quorum entitled to take action (s 215(c)(4))? Returns nothing for a stock corporation, or if the counts cannot be a vote.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the number of members of the class or group` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members does the class or group have?
      `the number of those members present in person or represented by proxy` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them are present in person or represented by proxy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the class or group of members have a quorum` IS
    IF `the kind is a nonstock corporation` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN `s 215(c)(4) the class or group has a quorum entitled to take action on the matter` `the number of members of the class or group` `the number of those members present in person or represented by proxy`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:805 | (4) Where a separate vote by a class or group or classes or groups is required, a majority of the members of such class or group or classes or groups, present in person or represented by proxy, shall constitute a quorum entitled to take action with respect to that vote on that matter and, in all matters other than the election of members of the governing body, the affirmative vote of the majority of the members of such class or group or classes or groups present in person or represented by proxy at the meeting shall be the act of such class or group or classes or groups.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(c)(4) (src:805)
@export Is the matter the act of the class or group of members, by a majority of its members present (s 215(c)(4))? Returns nothing for a stock corporation, or if the counts cannot be a vote.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the number of members of the class or group present in person or represented by proxy at the meeting` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members of the class or group are present in person or represented by proxy?
      `the number of those members in favor` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them are in favor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the matter the act of the class or group of members` IS
    IF `the kind is a nonstock corporation` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN `s 215(c)(4) the matter is the act of the class or group` `the number of members of the class or group present in person or represented by proxy at the meeting` `the number of those members in favor`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:806 | If the election of the governing body of any nonstock corporation shall not be held on the day designated by the bylaws, the governing body shall cause the election to be held as soon thereafter as convenient. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(d) (src:806)
@export If the election of the governing body was not held on the day the bylaws designate, must the governing body cause it to be held as soon thereafter as convenient (s 215(d))? Returns nothing for a stock corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the election was not held on the day designated by the bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the election of the governing body not held on the day the bylaws designate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the governing body cause the election to be held` IS
    IF `the kind is a nonstock corporation` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 215(d) the governing body must cause the election to be held as soon thereafter as convenient` `the election was not held on the day designated by the bylaws`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:806 | The failure to hold such an election at the designated time shall not work any forfeiture or dissolution of the corporation, but the Court of Chancery may summarily order such an election to be held upon the application of any member of the corporation. At any election pursuant to such order the persons entitled to vote in such election who shall be present at such meeting, either in person or by proxy, shall constitute a quorum for such meeting, notwithstanding any provision of the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws of the corporation to the contrary.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(d) (src:806)
@export Does a failure to hold the election of the governing body at the designated time work a forfeiture or dissolution of the corporation (s 215(d))? Returns nothing if there was no such failure, or for a stock corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the election was not held at the designated time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the election not held at the designated time?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the failure to hold the election work a forfeiture or dissolution` IS
    IF `the kind is a nonstock corporation` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN `s 215(d) the failure to hold the election at the designated time works a forfeiture or dissolution of the corporation` `the election was not held at the designated time`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:806 | but the Court of Chancery may summarily order such an election to be held upon the application of any member of the corporation. At any election pursuant to such order the persons entitled to vote in such election who shall be present at such meeting, either in person or by proxy, shall constitute a quorum for such meeting, notwithstanding any provision of the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws of the corporation to the contrary.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(d) (src:806)
@export As a member, may I ask the Court of Chancery to order the election of the governing body to be held (s 215(d))? Unlike section 211(c), the text names no waiting period. Returns nothing for a stock corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the election was not held on the day designated by the bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the election not held on the day the bylaws designate?
      `I am a member of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask the Court of Chancery to order the election` IS
    IF `the kind is a nonstock corporation` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 215(d) the Court of Chancery may summarily order the election to be held` `the election was not held on the day designated by the bylaws` `I am a member of the corporation`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:806 | At any election pursuant to such order the persons entitled to vote in such election who shall be present at such meeting, either in person or by proxy, shall constitute a quorum for such meeting, notwithstanding any provision of the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws of the corporation to the contrary.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(d) (src:806)
@export Do the persons entitled to vote who are present at an election the Court ordered constitute a quorum, despite the certificate or bylaws (s 215(d))? Returns nothing if no one is present, or for a stock corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the number of persons entitled to vote who are present at the election in person or by proxy` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons entitled to vote are present at the election, in person or by proxy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the persons present at the court-ordered election form a quorum` IS
    IF `the kind is a nonstock corporation` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN `s 215(d) the persons entitled to vote who are present constitute a quorum at the election the Court ordered` `the number of persons entitled to vote who are present at the election in person or by proxy`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:807 | (e) If authorized by the governing body, any requirement of a written ballot shall be satisfied by a ballot submitted by electronic transmission, provided that any such electronic transmission must either set forth or be submitted with information from which it can be determined that the electronic transmission was authorized by the member or proxy holder.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(e) (src:807)
@export Does a member's ballot submitted by electronic transmission satisfy any requirement of a written ballot (s 215(e))? Returns nothing for a stock corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the governing body has authorized ballots by electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the governing body authorized ballots by electronic transmission?
      `the electronic transmission sets forth, or is submitted with, information showing it was authorized by the member or proxy holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the transmission set forth, or is it submitted with, information from which it can be determined that the member or proxy holder authorized it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my electronic ballot satisfy a requirement of a written ballot as a member` IS
    IF `the kind is a nonstock corporation` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 215(e) a ballot submitted by electronic transmission satisfies any requirement of a written ballot` `the governing body has authorized ballots by electronic transmission` `the electronic transmission sets forth, or is submitted with, information showing it was authorized by the member or proxy holder`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:808 | (f) Except as otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation, in the bylaws, or by resolution of the governing body, the record date for any meeting or corporate action shall be deemed to be the date of such meeting or corporate action; provided, however, that no record date may precede any action by the governing body fixing such record date.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(f) (src:808)
@export What is the record date for a meeting or corporate action of a nonstock corporation (s 215(f))? The date of the meeting or action, unless the certificate, bylaws or a resolution of the governing body provides otherwise. Returns nothing for a stock corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the certificate, the bylaws or a resolution of the governing body provides a record date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the certificate of incorporation, the bylaws or a resolution of the governing body provide a record date?
      `the record date they provide` IS A DATE @desc What is it? (ignored if they provide none)
      `the day of the meeting or corporate action` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the meeting or action?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `What is the record date for a meeting or action of a nonstock corporation` IS
    IF `the kind is a nonstock corporation` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 215(f) the record date for the meeting or corporate action` provided `the day of the meeting or corporate action`)
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        provided MEANS IF `the certificate, the bylaws or a resolution of the governing body provides a record date` THEN JUST `the record date they provide` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:808 | (f) Except as otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation, in the bylaws, or by resolution of the governing body, the record date for any meeting or corporate action shall be deemed to be the date of such meeting or corporate action; provided, however, that no record date may precede any action by the governing body fixing such record date.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(f) (src:808)
@export May this day be the record date, given that no record date may precede the governing body's action fixing it (s 215(f))? Returns nothing for a stock corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the day proposed as the record date` IS A DATE @desc What day is proposed as the record date?
      `the day of the action of the governing body fixing the record date` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the governing body act to fix it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the record date precede the governing body's action fixing it` IS
    IF `the kind is a nonstock corporation` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 215(f) the record date does not precede the action of the governing body fixing it` `the day proposed as the record date` `the day of the action of the governing body fixing the record date`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 216 Quorum and vote at a stockholders' meeting`

-- src:812 | Subject to this chapter in respect of the vote that shall be required for a specified action, the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of any corporation authorized to issue stock may specify the number of shares and/or the amount of other securities having voting power the holders of which shall be present or represented by proxy at any meeting in order to constitute a quorum for, and the votes that shall be necessary for, the transaction of any business, but in no event shall a quorum consist of less than 1/3 of the shares entitled to vote at the meeting, except that, where a separate vote by a class or series or classes or series is required, a quorum shall consist of no less than 1/3 of the shares of such class or series or classes or series. …
-- src:813 | (1) A majority of the shares entitled to vote, present in person or represented by proxy, shall constitute a quorum at a meeting of stockholders;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 216 (src:812); § 216(1) (src:813)
@export Is a quorum present at the meeting of stockholders (s 216)? A majority of the votes entitled, unless the certificate or bylaws set the quorum, which can never be less than one-third. Returns nothing for a nonstock corporation, or if the counts cannot be a vote.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws specify a quorum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws specify the number of votes that must be present or represented by proxy to constitute a quorum?
      `the number of votes they specify` IS A NUMBER @desc How many? (ignored if they specify none)
      `the number of votes entitled to vote at the meeting, or of the class or series voting separately` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes are entitled to vote at the meeting (or, for a class or series voting separately, held by that class or series)?
      `the number of votes present in person or represented by proxy` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes are present in person or represented by proxy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a quorum present at the stockholders' meeting` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 216 of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN `s 216 a quorum is present` specified `the number of votes entitled to vote at the meeting, or of the class or series voting separately` `the number of votes present in person or represented by proxy`
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        specified MEANS IF `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws specify a quorum` THEN JUST `the number of votes they specify` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:814 | (2) In all matters other than the election of directors, the affirmative vote of the majority of shares present in person or represented by proxy at the meeting and entitled to vote on the subject matter shall be the act of the stockholders;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 216(2) (src:814)
@export Is a matter other than the election of directors the act of the stockholders (s 216(2))? A majority of the votes present and entitled to vote on it, unless the Law requires or the certificate or bylaws specify another vote. Returns nothing for a nonstock corporation, or if the counts cannot be a vote.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `a vote other than a majority of the votes present applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Law require, or do the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws specify, a vote other than the default (a majority of the votes present and entitled to vote on the subject matter)? Give the one that applies: the Law's, if it requires one.
      `the numerator of the fraction required` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the fraction of the votes required: the numerator? (for two-thirds, 2; ignored if the default applies)
      `the denominator of the fraction required` IS A NUMBER @desc The denominator? (for two-thirds, 3; ignored if the default applies)
      `the fraction must be exceeded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Must the fraction be exceeded ("a majority"), rather than merely reached ("at least")? (ignored if the default applies)
      `the fraction is of the votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the fraction of the outstanding votes entitled to vote, rather than of the votes present? (ignored if the default applies)
      `the number of votes in favor` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes are in favor?
      `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes does the outstanding stock entitled to vote hold in all?
      `the number of votes present in person or represented by proxy and entitled to vote on the subject matter` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes are present in person or by proxy and entitled to vote on the subject matter?
      `the number of votes cast` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the matter the act of the stockholders` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 216 of this title` `the kind of corporation`)) THEN NOTHING
        IF invalidFraction THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE `s 216(2) the matter is the act of the stockholders` (`s 216 the vote that is necessary for a matter other than the election of directors` appliedVote NOTHING) `the number of votes in favor` `the number of votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote` `the number of votes present in person or represented by proxy and entitled to vote on the subject matter` `the number of votes cast`
    WHERE
        appliedVote MEANS IF `a vote other than a majority of the votes present applies` THEN JUST requirement ELSE NOTHING
        requirement MEANS `Vote requirement` WITH
            `counted against` IS base
            proportion IS fraction
            `must be exceeded` IS `the fraction must be exceeded`
        base MEANS IF `the fraction is of the votes of the outstanding stock entitled to vote` THEN `the outstanding stock entitled to vote` ELSE `the shares present in person or represented by proxy and entitled to vote`
        fraction MEANS IF `the denominator of the fraction required` GREATER THAN 0 THEN `the numerator of the fraction required` DIVIDED BY `the denominator of the fraction required` ELSE 0
        invalidFraction MEANS `a vote other than a majority of the votes present applies` AND `the denominator of the fraction required` AT MOST 0

-- src:815 | (3) Directors shall be elected by a plurality of the votes of the shares present in person or represented by proxy at the meeting and entitled to vote on the election of directors; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 216(3) (src:815)
@export Am I elected a director by a plurality of the votes of the shares present and entitled to vote on the election (s 216(3))? Returns nothing for a nonstock corporation, or if there is a tie for the last place.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the votes for me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast for you?
      `the votes for each other candidate` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast for each other candidate?
      `the number of directors to be elected` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors are to be elected?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I elected director by a plurality of the votes` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 216 of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN `s 216(3) the candidate is elected by a plurality of the votes` `the votes for me` `the votes for each other candidate` `the number of directors to be elected`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:816 | (4) Where a separate vote by a class or series or classes or series is required, a majority of the outstanding shares of such class or series or classes or series, present in person or represented by proxy, shall constitute a quorum entitled to take action with respect to that vote on that matter and, in all matters other than the election of directors, the affirmative vote of the majority of shares of such class or series or classes or series present in person or represented by proxy at the meeting shall be the act of such class or series or classes or series.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 216(4) (src:816)
@export Where a separate vote by a class or series is required, is a majority of the outstanding shares of the class or series present, so that it has a quorum entitled to take action (s 216(4))? Returns nothing for a nonstock corporation, or if the counts cannot be a vote.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the number of votes of the outstanding shares of the class or series` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes do the outstanding shares of the class or series hold?
      `the number of those votes present in person or represented by proxy` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those votes are present in person or represented by proxy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the class or series have a quorum entitled to act` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 216 of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN `s 216(4) the class or series has a quorum entitled to take action on the matter` `the number of votes of the outstanding shares of the class or series` `the number of those votes present in person or represented by proxy`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:816 | (4) Where a separate vote by a class or series or classes or series is required, a majority of the outstanding shares of such class or series or classes or series, present in person or represented by proxy, shall constitute a quorum entitled to take action with respect to that vote on that matter and, in all matters other than the election of directors, the affirmative vote of the majority of shares of such class or series or classes or series present in person or represented by proxy at the meeting shall be the act of such class or series or classes or series.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 216(4) (src:816)
@export Is a matter other than the election of directors the act of the class or series, by a majority of its shares present (s 216(4))? Returns nothing for a nonstock corporation, or if the counts cannot be a vote.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the number of votes of the class or series present in person or represented by proxy at the meeting` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes of the class or series are present in person or represented by proxy at the meeting?
      `the number of those votes in favor` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them are in favor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the matter the act of the class or series` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 216 of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN `s 216(4) the matter is the act of the class or series` `the number of votes of the class or series present in person or represented by proxy at the meeting` `the number of those votes in favor`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:817 | A bylaw amendment adopted by stockholders which specifies the votes that shall be necessary for the election of directors shall not be further amended or repealed by the board of directors.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 216 (src:817)
@export May the board of directors further amend or repeal a bylaw amendment adopted by the stockholders that specifies the votes necessary for the election of directors (s 216, last sentence)? Returns nothing for any other bylaw, or for a nonstock corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the bylaw amendment was adopted by stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the bylaw amendment adopted by the stockholders?
      `the bylaw amendment specifies the votes necessary for the election of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it specify the votes that are necessary for the election of directors?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the board amend or repeal a bylaw the stockholders adopted on director elections` IS
    IF `s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` `section 216 of this title` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN `s 216 the board of directors may further amend or repeal the bylaw amendment` `the bylaw amendment was adopted by stockholders` `the bylaw amendment specifies the votes necessary for the election of directors`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 114 (read for these sections in the group for s 215) says whether they apply to my kind of corporation: s 217 and s 218(a) and (b) not to a nonprofit
-- nonstock corporation; s 219 only to a stock corporation. The questions return nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
§ `s 217, s 218 and s 219: fiduciaries and joint owners, voting trusts and agreements, the list of stockholders`

§§ `s 217 Voting the shares as fiduciary, pledgor, pledgee or joint owner`

-- src:206 | (2) Sections 102(b)(3), 111(a)(2) and (3), 144(a)(2), 217, 218(a) and (b), and 262 of this title; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(c)(2) (src:206)
@export Does section 217 (voting rights of fiduciaries, pledgors and joint owners of stock) apply to my kind of corporation?
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 217 apply to my corporation` IF
    `s 217 the section applies to the kind of corporation` `the kind of corporation`

-- src:821 | (a) Persons holding stock in a fiduciary capacity shall be entitled to vote the shares so held. Persons whose stock is pledged shall be entitled to vote, unless in the transfer by the pledgor on the books of the corporation such person has expressly empowered the pledgee to vote thereon, in which case only the pledgee, or such pledgee’s proxy, may represent such stock and vote thereon.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 217(a) (src:821)
@export Am I entitled to vote the shares, as a fiduciary, as a pledgor, or as a pledgee (s 217(a))? Returns nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the capacity in which I would vote the shares` IS A `s 217(a) Capacity in which the person would vote the shares` @desc In what capacity would you vote the shares: as a person holding the stock in a fiduciary capacity; as a person whose stock is pledged; or as the pledgee of the stock, or the pledgee's proxy?
      `the pledgor expressly empowered the pledgee to vote the stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the transfer by the pledgor on the books of the corporation, did the pledgor expressly empower the pledgee to vote the stock?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to vote the shares` IS
    IF `s 217 the section applies to the kind of corporation` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 217(a) the person is entitled to vote the shares` `the capacity in which I would vote the shares` `the pledgor expressly empowered the pledgee to vote the stock`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:822 | (b) If shares or other securities having voting power stand of record in the names of 2 or more persons, whether fiduciaries, members of a partnership, joint tenants, tenants in common, tenants by the entirety or otherwise, or if 2 or more persons have the same fiduciary relationship respecting the same shares, unless the secretary of the corporation is given written notice to the contrary and is furnished with a copy of the instrument or order appointing them or creating the relationship wherein it is so provided, their acts with respect to voting shall have the following effect:
-- src:823 | (1) If only 1 votes, such person’s act binds all;
-- src:824 | (2) If more than 1 vote, the act of the majority so voting binds all;
-- src:825 | (3) If more than 1 vote, but the vote is evenly split on any particular matter, each faction may vote the securities in question proportionally, or any person voting the shares, or a beneficiary, if any, may apply to the Court of Chancery or such other court as may have jurisdiction to appoint an additional person to act with the persons so voting the shares, which shall then be voted as determined by a majority of such persons and the person appointed by the Court. If the instrument so filed shows that any such tenancy is held in unequal interests, a majority or even split for the purpose of this subsection shall be a majority or even split in interest.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 217(b) (src:822-825)
@export When shares stand of record in the names of two or more persons, what is the effect of how they vote (s 217(b))? Returns nothing if no one votes, or if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the secretary of the corporation was given written notice to the contrary and the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the secretary of the corporation given written notice to the contrary and furnished with a copy of the instrument or order appointing you or creating the relationship, in which it is so provided?
      `the instrument filed shows that the tenancy is held in unequal interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the instrument filed show that the tenancy is held in unequal interests?
      `the number of the persons who vote` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the persons in whose names the shares stand vote?
      `the number of those persons who vote one way` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them vote one way?
      `the number of those persons who vote the other way` IS A NUMBER @desc How many vote the other way?
      `the interest of those who vote one way` IS A NUMBER @desc If the interests are unequal, what is the combined interest of those voting one way? (ignored if equal)
      `the interest of those who vote the other way` IS A NUMBER @desc And of those voting the other way? (ignored if equal)
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 217(b) Effect of the voting of persons in whose names the shares stand`
DECIDE `What is the effect of the voting of the persons in whose names the shares stand` IS
    IF `s 217 the section applies to the kind of corporation` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN `s 217(b) the effect of the voting of the persons in whose names the shares stand` `the secretary of the corporation was given written notice to the contrary and the instrument` `the instrument filed shows that the tenancy is held in unequal interests` `the number of the persons who vote` `the number of those persons who vote one way` `the number of those persons who vote the other way` `the interest of those who vote one way` `the interest of those who vote the other way`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:825 | If more than 1 vote, but the vote is evenly split on any particular matter, each faction may vote the securities in question proportionally, or any person voting the shares, or a beneficiary, if any, may apply to the Court of Chancery or such other court as may have jurisdiction to appoint an additional person to act with the persons so voting the shares, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 217(b)(3) (src:825)
@export If the persons voting the shares are evenly split, may I apply to the Court of Chancery or another court to appoint an additional person to act with them (s 217(b)(3))? Returns nothing if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the vote is evenly split on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the vote evenly split on the matter?
      `I am one of the persons voting the shares, or a beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you one of the persons voting the shares, or a beneficiary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to a court to appoint an additional person to vote the shares` IS
    IF `s 217 the section applies to the kind of corporation` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 217(b)(3) the person may apply to the Court of Chancery or another court with jurisdiction to appoint an additional person` `the vote is evenly split on the matter` `I am one of the persons voting the shares, or a beneficiary`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:825 | which shall then be voted as determined by a majority of such persons and the person appointed by the Court. If the instrument so filed shows that any such tenancy is held in unequal interests, a majority or even split for the purpose of this subsection shall be a majority or even split in interest.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 217(b)(3) (src:825)
@export Once the court appoints an additional person, are the shares voted in favor, as determined by a majority of the persons voting and the person appointed (s 217(b)(3))? Returns nothing if the counts cannot be a vote, or if the section does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the number of the persons so voting and the person appointed by the court` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons are there in all, counting the person the court appointed?
      `the number of them who are in favor` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them are in favor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `How are the shares voted once the court appoints an additional person` IS
    IF `s 217 the section applies to the kind of corporation` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN `s 217(b)(3) the shares are voted in favor as determined by a majority of the persons so voting and the person appointed` `the number of the persons so voting and the person appointed by the court` `the number of them who are in favor`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 218 Voting trusts and voting agreements`

-- src:206 | (2) Sections 102(b)(3), 111(a)(2) and (3), 144(a)(2), 217, 218(a) and (b), and 262 of this title; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(c)(2) (src:206)
@export Do sections 218(a) and (b) (the voting trust) apply to my kind of corporation?
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do sections 218(a) and (b) apply to my corporation` IF
    `s 218(a) and (b) apply to the kind of corporation` `the kind of corporation`

-- src:829 | One stockholder or 2 or more stockholders may by agreement in writing deposit capital stock of an original issue with or transfer capital stock to any person or persons, or entity or entities authorized to act as trustee, for the purpose of vesting in such person or persons, entity or entities, who may be designated voting trustee, or voting trustees, the right to vote thereon for any period of time determined by such agreement, upon the terms and conditions stated in such agreement. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 218(a) (src:829)
@export Does our agreement create a voting trust under section 218(a)? Returns nothing if the subsection does not apply to my kind of corporation.
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `the agreement is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement in writing?
      `the stock is capital stock of an original issue deposited with, or capital stock transferred to, a person or entity authorized to act as trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the stock capital stock of an original issue deposited with, or capital stock transferred to, a person or entity authorized to act as trustee?
      `the purpose is to vest in the voting trustee the right to vote on the stock for a period of time the agreement determines` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose to vest in the voting trustee the right to vote on the stock for a period of time the agreement determines?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our agreement create a voting trust` IS
    IF `s 218(a) and (b) apply to the kind of corporation` `the kind of corporation`
    THEN JUST (`s 218(a) the agreement creates a voting trust` `the agreement is in writing` `the stock is capital stock of an original issue deposited with, or capital stock transferred to, a person or entity authorized to act as trustee` `the purpose is to vest in the voting trustee the right to vote on the stock for a period of time the agreement determines`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:829 | After delivery of a copy of the agreement to the registered office of the corporation in this State or the principal place of business of the corporation, which copy shall be open to the inspection of any stockholder of the corporation or any beneficiary of the trust under the agreement daily during business hours, certificates of stock or uncertificated stock shall be issued to the voting trustee or trustees to represent any stock of an original issue so deposited with such voting trustee or trustees, and any certificates of stock or uncertificated stock so transferred to the voting trustee or trustees shall be surrendered and cancelled and new certificates or uncertificated stock shall be issued therefore to the voting trustee or trustees. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 218(a) (src:829)
@export Must the corporation issue certificates or uncertificated stock to the voting trustee in place of the stock deposited or transferred (s 218(a))? Returns nothing if the subsection does not apply to my kind of corporation.
