-- Section 220 is not on the lists of s 114(b) or (c), so it applies to every kind of corporation, with members for stockholders.
-- Situation: I want to inspect the corporation's books and records, or the corporation has refused or ignored my demand.
§ `s 220 Inspection of books and records`

§§ `s 220(a) Definitions: records, purpose, stockholder, subsidiary, oath`

-- src:843 | (1) “Books and records” means all of the following:
-- src:844 | a. The “certificate of incorporation,” as defined in § 104 of this title, including a copy of any agreement or other instrument incorporated by reference in the certificate of incorporation.
-- src:845 | b. The bylaws then in effect, including a copy of any agreement or other instrument incorporated by reference in the bylaws.
-- src:846 | c. Minutes of all meetings of stockholders and the signed consents evidencing all action taken by stockholders without a meeting, in each case for the 3 years preceding the date of the demand under subsection (b) of this section.
-- src:847 | d. All communications in writing or by electronic transmission to stockholders generally within the past 3 years preceding the date of the demand under subsection (b) of this section.
-- src:848 | e. Minutes of any meeting of the board of directors or any committee of the board of directors and records of any action of the board of directors or any such committee.
-- src:849 | f. Materials provided to the board of directors or any committee of the board of directors in connection with actions taken by the board of directors or any such committee.
-- src:850 | g. Annual financial statements of the corporation for the 3 years preceding the date of the demand under subsection (b) of this section.
-- src:851 | h. Any agreement entered into under § 122(18) of this title.
-- src:852 | i. Director and officer independence questionnaires.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(a)(1) (src:843-852)
@export Is this record among the "books and records" a stockholder may demand to inspect (s 220(a)(1))?
GIVEN `the kind of record` IS A `s 220(a)(1) Kind of record` @desc Which kind of record: the certificate of incorporation (with instruments incorporated by reference); the bylaws; minutes of stockholder meetings and signed consents; communications to stockholders generally; board or committee minutes and records of action; materials given to the board or a committee; annual financial statements; an agreement under section 122(18); director and officer independence questionnaires; or any other record?
      `the date of the record` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the record (the meeting or consent, the communication, or the end of the year the statements are for)?
      `the date of the demand` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the demand made?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this record among the books and records I may demand` IF
    `s 220(a)(1) the record is among the books and records` `the kind of record` `the date of the record` `the date of the demand`

-- src:853 | (2) “Proper purpose” means a purpose reasonably related to a stockholder’s interest as a stockholder.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(a)(2) (src:853)
@export Is my purpose a proper purpose, being reasonably related to my interest as a stockholder (s 220(a)(2))?
GIVEN `the purpose is reasonably related to my interest as a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your purpose reasonably related to your interest as a stockholder?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my purpose a proper purpose` IF
    `s 220(a)(2) the purpose is a proper purpose` `the purpose is reasonably related to my interest as a stockholder`

-- src:854 | (3) “Stockholder” means a person who is a holder of record of stock in a stock corporation, or a person who is the beneficial owner of shares of such stock held either in a voting trust or by a nominee on behalf of such person.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(a)(3) (src:854)
@export Am I a stockholder for the purposes of section 220 (s 220(a)(3))?
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
      `I am a holder of record of stock in the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a holder of record of stock in the corporation?
      `I am the beneficial owner of shares of such stock held in a voting trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the beneficial owner of shares of such stock held in a voting trust?
      `I am the beneficial owner of shares of such stock held by a nominee on my behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the beneficial owner of shares of such stock held by a nominee on your behalf?
      `I am a member of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the corporation (if it is a nonstock corporation)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a stockholder for the purposes of section 220` IF
    `s 220(a)(3) the person is a stockholder for the purposes of this section` `the kind of corporation` `I am a holder of record of stock in the corporation` `I am the beneficial owner of shares of such stock held in a voting trust` `I am the beneficial owner of shares of such stock held by a nominee on my behalf` `I am a member of the corporation`

-- src:855 | (4) “Subsidiary” means any entity directly or indirectly owned, in whole or in part, by the corporation of which the stockholder is a stockholder and over the affairs of which the corporation directly or indirectly exercises control, and includes, without limitation, corporations, partnerships, limited partnerships, limited liability partnerships, limited liability companies, statutory trusts and/or joint ventures.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(a)(4) (src:855)
@export Is this entity a subsidiary of the corporation for the purposes of section 220 (s 220(a)(4))?
GIVEN `the entity is directly or indirectly owned, in whole or in part, by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entity directly or indirectly owned, in whole or in part, by the corporation of which you are a stockholder?
      `the corporation directly or indirectly exercises control over the affairs of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation directly or indirectly exercise control over the affairs of the entity?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this entity a subsidiary of the corporation` IF
    `s 220(a)(4) the entity is a subsidiary` `the entity is directly or indirectly owned, in whole or in part, by the corporation` `the corporation directly or indirectly exercises control over the affairs of the entity`

-- src:856 | (5) “Under oath” includes statements the declarant affirms to be true under penalty of perjury under the laws of the United States or any state.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(a)(5) (src:856)
@export Is my statement under oath for the purposes of section 220 (s 220(a)(5))? A statement affirmed to be true under penalty of perjury under the laws of the United States or any state is.
GIVEN `the statement is made under oath in the ordinary sense` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement made under oath in the ordinary sense?
      `I affirm the statement to be true under penalty of perjury under the laws of the United States or any state` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you affirm the statement to be true under penalty of perjury under the laws of the United States or any state?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my statement under oath` IF
    `s 220(a)(5) the statement is under oath` `the statement is made under oath in the ordinary sense` `I affirm the statement to be true under penalty of perjury under the laws of the United States or any state`

§§ `s 220(b) My right to inspect, and the corporation's right to impose conditions`

-- src:872 | (5) In every instance where the stockholder is other than a record holder of stock in a stock corporation, or a member of a nonstock corporation, the demand under oath shall state the person’s status as a stockholder, be accompanied by documentary evidence of beneficial ownership of the stock, and state that such documentary evidence is a true and correct copy of what it purports to be.
-- src:873 | (6) In every instance where an attorney or other agent shall be the person who seeks the right to inspection, the demand under oath shall be accompanied by a power of attorney or such other writing which authorizes the attorney or other agent to so act on behalf of the stockholder.
-- src:874 | (7) The demand under oath shall be directed to the corporation at its registered office in this State or at its principal place of business.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(b)(5) (src:872); § 220(b)(6) (src:873); § 220(b)(7) (src:874)
@export Does my demand comply with section 220 respecting the form and manner of making demand (s 220(b)(1), (5), (6) and (7))?
GIVEN `the demand is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the demand in writing?
      `the demand is under oath` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it under oath?
      `I am other than a record holder of stock in a stock corporation or a member of a nonstock corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you other than a record holder of stock in a stock corporation, or a member of a nonstock corporation (for example a beneficial owner)?
      `the demand states my status as a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does the demand state your status as a stockholder?
      `the demand is accompanied by documentary evidence of beneficial ownership of the stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it accompanied by documentary evidence of your beneficial ownership of the stock?
      `the demand states that the documentary evidence is a true and correct copy of what it purports to be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that the documentary evidence is a true and correct copy of what it purports to be?
      `an attorney or other agent seeks the inspection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an attorney or other agent seeking the inspection for you?
      `the demand is accompanied by a power of attorney or other writing authorizing the attorney or agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, is the demand accompanied by a power of attorney or other writing authorizing the attorney or agent to act for you?
      `the demand is directed to the corporation at its registered office or its principal place of business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the demand directed to the corporation at its registered office in this State or at its principal place of business?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my demand comply with the form and manner section 220 requires` IF
    `s 220(b) the demand complies with this section respecting the form and manner of making demand` demand
    WHERE
        demand MEANS `s 220(b) Demand` WITH
            `the demand is in writing` IS `the demand is in writing`
            `the demand is under oath` IS `the demand is under oath`
            `the person is other than a record holder of stock in a stock corporation or a member of a nonstock corporation` IS `I am other than a record holder of stock in a stock corporation or a member of a nonstock corporation`
            `the demand states the person's status as a stockholder` IS `the demand states my status as a stockholder`
            `the demand is accompanied by documentary evidence of beneficial ownership of the stock` IS `the demand is accompanied by documentary evidence of beneficial ownership of the stock`
            `the demand states that the documentary evidence is a true and correct copy of what it purports to be` IS `the demand states that the documentary evidence is a true and correct copy of what it purports to be`
            `an attorney or other agent seeks the inspection` IS `an attorney or other agent seeks the inspection`
            `the demand is accompanied by a power of attorney or other writing authorizing the attorney or agent` IS `the demand is accompanied by a power of attorney or other writing authorizing the attorney or agent`
            `the demand is directed to the corporation at its registered office in this State or at its principal place of business` IS `the demand is directed to the corporation at its registered office or its principal place of business`

-- src:864 | (2) A stockholder may inspect and copy the corporation’s books and records only if all of the following apply:
-- src:865 | a. The stockholder’s demand is made in good faith and for a proper purpose.
-- src:866 | b. The stockholder’s demand describes with reasonable particularity the stockholder’s purpose and the books and records the stockholder seeks to inspect.
-- src:867 | c. The books and records sought are specifically related to the stockholder’s purpose.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(b)(2) (src:864-867)
@export Are the conditions of section 220(b)(2) for inspecting and copying the corporation's books and records met?
GIVEN `the demand is made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the demand made in good faith?
      `my purpose is a proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your purpose a proper purpose?
      `the demand describes my purpose with reasonable particularity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the demand describe your purpose with reasonable particularity?
      `the demand describes the books and records I seek with reasonable particularity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it describe the books and records you seek with reasonable particularity?
      `the books and records I seek are specifically related to my purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the books and records you seek specifically related to your purpose?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the conditions for inspecting the corporation's books and records met` IF
    `s 220(b)(2) the conditions for inspecting and copying the corporation's books and records are met` `the demand is made in good faith` `my purpose is a proper purpose` `the demand describes my purpose with reasonable particularity` `the demand describes the books and records I seek with reasonable particularity` `the books and records I seek are specifically related to my purpose`

-- src:857 | (b) (1) Subject to paragraph (b)(2) of this section, any stockholder, in person or by attorney or other agent, shall, upon written demand under oath, have the right during the usual hours for business to inspect for any proper purpose, and to make copies and extracts from:
-- src:858 | a. The corporation’s stock ledger, a list of its stockholders, and its other books and records; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(b)(1) (src:857-858)
@export Do I have the right to inspect and copy the corporation's stock ledger and a list of its stockholders (s 220(b)(1))?
GIVEN `I am a stockholder for the purposes of section 220` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a stockholder for the purposes of section 220?
      `my demand complies with section 220 respecting the form and manner of making demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your demand comply with section 220 respecting the form and manner of making demand?
      `my purpose is a proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your purpose a proper purpose?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I inspect and copy the stock ledger and the list of stockholders` IF
    `s 220(b)(1)a. the stockholder has the right to inspect and copy the stock ledger and the list of stockholders` `I am a stockholder for the purposes of section 220` `my demand complies with section 220 respecting the form and manner of making demand` `my purpose is a proper purpose`

-- src:857 | (b) (1) Subject to paragraph (b)(2) of this section, any stockholder, in person or by attorney or other agent, shall, upon written demand under oath, have the right during the usual hours for business to inspect for any proper purpose, and to make copies and extracts from:
-- src:858 | a. The corporation’s stock ledger, a list of its stockholders, and its other books and records; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(b)(1) (src:857-858); § 220(b)(2) (src:864-867)
@export Do I have the right to inspect and copy the corporation's books and records (s 220(b)(1) and (2))?
GIVEN `I am a stockholder for the purposes of section 220` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a stockholder for the purposes of section 220?
      `my demand complies with section 220 respecting the form and manner of making demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your demand comply with section 220 respecting the form and manner of making demand?
      `the conditions of section 220(b)(2) are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the conditions of section 220(b)(2) met?
      `the record is among the books and records` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the record among the "books and records" defined in section 220(a)(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I inspect and copy the corporation's books and records` IF
    `s 220(b)(1)a. the stockholder has the right to inspect and copy the corporation's books and records` `I am a stockholder for the purposes of section 220` `my demand complies with section 220 respecting the form and manner of making demand` `the conditions of section 220(b)(2) are met` `the record is among the books and records`

-- src:859 | b. A subsidiary’s books and records, to the extent that:
-- src:860 | 1. The corporation has actual possession and control of such records of such subsidiary; or
-- src:861 | 2. The corporation could obtain such records through the exercise of control over such subsidiary, provided that as of the date of the making of the demand:
-- src:862 | A. The stockholder inspection of such books and records of the subsidiary would not constitute a breach of an agreement between the corporation or the subsidiary and a person or persons not affiliated with the corporation; and
-- src:863 | B. The subsidiary would not have the right under the law applicable to it to deny the corporation access to such books and records upon demand by the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(b)(1) (src:859-863)
@export Do I have the right to inspect and copy a subsidiary's books and records (s 220(b)(1)b.)?
GIVEN `I may inspect and copy the corporation's books and records` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the right to inspect and copy the corporation's books and records?
      `the corporation has actual possession and control of the subsidiary's records` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation have actual possession and control of the subsidiary's records?
      `the corporation could obtain the subsidiary's records through the exercise of control over the subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could the corporation obtain them through the exercise of control over the subsidiary?
      `inspection would not breach an agreement between the corporation or the subsidiary and a person not affiliated with the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As of the date of the demand, would inspection not breach an agreement between the corporation or the subsidiary and a person not affiliated with the corporation?
      `the subsidiary would not have the right under the law applicable to it to deny the corporation access on demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As of the date of the demand, would the subsidiary not have the right under the law applicable to it to deny the corporation access on demand?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I inspect and copy a subsidiary's books and records` IF
    `s 220(b)(1)b. the stockholder has the right to inspect and copy the subsidiary's books and records` `I may inspect and copy the corporation's books and records` `the corporation has actual possession and control of the subsidiary's records` `the corporation could obtain the subsidiary's records through the exercise of control over the subsidiary` `inspection would not breach an agreement between the corporation or the subsidiary and a person not affiliated with the corporation` `the subsidiary would not have the right under the law applicable to it to deny the corporation access on demand`

-- src:868 | (3) The corporation may impose reasonable restrictions on the confidentiality, use, or distribution of books and records and may require, as a condition to producing books and records to a stockholder under any demand under this subsection, that the stockholder agree that any information included in the corporation’s books and records is deemed incorporated by reference in any complaint filed by or at the direction of the stockholder in relation to the subject matter referenced in the demand. The corporation may redact portions of any books and records produced to such stockholder under this subsection to the extent the portions so redacted are not specifically related to the stockholder’s purpose.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(b)(3) (src:868)
@export May the corporation impose this condition on producing books and records to me, or redact part of what it produces (s 220(b)(3))?
GIVEN `the measure` IS A `s 220(b)(3) What the corporation may impose or do` @desc Which measure: reasonable restrictions on the confidentiality, use or distribution of the records; a requirement that you agree the information is incorporated by reference in any complaint you file about the subject of the demand; or redaction of a portion?
      `a demand has been made under section 220(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a demand been made under section 220(b)?
      `the portion is specifically related to my purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a redaction: is the portion specifically related to your purpose?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation impose this condition or redact when it produces records to me` IF
    `s 220(b)(3) the corporation may do it` `the measure` `a demand has been made under section 220(b)` `the portion is specifically related to my purpose`

-- src:869 | (4) This section does not affect:
-- src:870 | a. The right of a stockholder to seek discovery of books and records if the stockholder is in litigation with the corporation, to the same extent as any other litigant; or
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(b)(4) (src:869-870)
@export Does section 220 affect my right to seek discovery of books and records from the corporation if I am in litigation with it (s 220(b)(4)a.)? Returns nothing if I am not in litigation with it.
GIVEN `I am in litigation with the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in litigation with the corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 220 affect my right to seek discovery of books and records in litigation` IS
    `s 220(b)(4)a. this section affects the stockholder's right to seek discovery of books and records from the corporation as any other litigant may` `I am in litigation with the corporation`

-- src:871 | b. The power of a court, independently of this chapter, to compel the production of corporate records for inspection and to impose reasonable restrictions as provided in paragraph (b)(3) of this section, provided that, in the case of production of “books and records” defined in subsection (a) of this section at the request of a stockholder, the stockholder has met the requirements of this subsection.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(b)(4) (src:871)
@export May a court compel the production of corporate records for inspection independently of the chapter (s 220(b)(4)b.)? If the records are "books and records" at a stockholder's request, only if the stockholder has met the requirements of section 220(b).
GIVEN `the production is of books and records defined in section 220(a), at the request of a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the production of "books and records" as defined in section 220(a), at the request of a stockholder?
      `the stockholder has met the requirements of section 220(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the stockholder met the requirements of section 220(b)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a court compel production of the corporation's records independently of section 220` IF
    `s 220(b)(4)b. the power of a court independently of this chapter to compel production of corporate records for inspection may be exercised` `the production is of books and records defined in section 220(a), at the request of a stockholder` `the stockholder has met the requirements of section 220(b)`

§§ `s 220(c) If the corporation refuses or does not reply: the Court of Chancery`

-- src:875 | If the corporation, or an officer or agent thereof, refuses to permit an inspection sought by a stockholder or attorney or other agent acting for the stockholder pursuant to subsection (b) of this section or does not reply to the demand within 5 business days after the demand has been made, the stockholder may apply to the Court of Chancery for an order to compel such inspection. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(c) (src:875)
@export May I apply to the Court of Chancery for an order to compel the inspection because the corporation refused, or did not reply within 5 business days after my demand (s 220(c))?
GIVEN `the corporation, or an officer or agent of it, refuses to permit the inspection I seek under section 220(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation, or an officer or agent of it, refuse to permit the inspection you seek under section 220(b)?
      `the corporation has replied to my demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation replied to your demand?
      `the number of business days after my demand that have ended` IS A NUMBER @desc How many business days after your demand was made have ended?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to the Court of Chancery to compel the inspection` IF
    `s 220(c) the stockholder may apply to the Court of Chancery for an order to compel the inspection` `the corporation, or an officer or agent of it, refuses to permit the inspection I seek under section 220(b)` `the corporation has replied to my demand` `the number of business days after my demand that have ended`

-- src:875 | The Court of Chancery is hereby vested with exclusive jurisdiction to determine whether or not the person seeking inspection is entitled to the inspection sought. The Court may summarily order the corporation to permit the stockholder to inspect the corporation’s stock ledger, an existing list of stockholders, and its other books and records, and to make copies or extracts therefrom; or the Court may order the corporation to furnish to the stockholder a list of its stockholders as of a specific date on condition that the stockholder first pay to the corporation the reasonable cost of obtaining and furnishing such list and on such other conditions as the Court deems appropriate. Where the stockholder seeks to inspect the corporation’s books and records, other than its stock ledger or list of stockholders, such stockholder shall first establish that:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(c) (src:875)
@export Does the court have jurisdiction to determine whether I am entitled to the inspection I seek? Only the Court of Chancery does (s 220(c)).
GIVEN `my action is brought in the Court of Chancery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your action brought in the Court of Chancery?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the court have jurisdiction to decide whether I am entitled to the inspection` IF
    `s 220(c) the court has jurisdiction to determine whether the person seeking inspection is entitled to the inspection sought` `my action is brought in the Court of Chancery`

-- src:875 | The Court may summarily order the corporation to permit the stockholder to inspect the corporation’s stock ledger, an existing list of stockholders, and its other books and records, and to make copies or extracts therefrom; or the Court may order the corporation to furnish to the stockholder a list of its stockholders as of a specific date on condition that the stockholder first pay to the corporation the reasonable cost of obtaining and furnishing such list and on such other conditions as the Court deems appropriate. …
-- src:879 | The Court may, in its discretion, prescribe any limitations or conditions with reference to the inspection, or award such other or further relief as the Court may deem just and proper. The Court may order books, documents and records, pertinent extracts therefrom, or duly authenticated copies thereof, to be brought within this State and kept in this State upon such terms and conditions as the order may prescribe.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(c) (src:875, 879)
@export May the Court of Chancery make this order on a stockholder's application under section 220(c)?
GIVEN `the order` IS A `s 220(c) Order the Court may make on a stockholder's application` @desc Which order: a summary order to permit inspection of the stock ledger, an existing list of stockholders and other books and records, with copies or extracts; an order to furnish a list of stockholders as of a specific date; a limitation or condition on the inspection; other or further relief; or an order that records be brought within and kept in this State?
      `the stockholder has applied under section 220(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the stockholder applied under section 220(c)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Court of Chancery make this order on my application` IF
    `s 220(c) the Court of Chancery may make the order` `the order` `the stockholder has applied under section 220(c)`

-- src:875 | or the Court may order the corporation to furnish to the stockholder a list of its stockholders as of a specific date on condition that the stockholder first pay to the corporation the reasonable cost of obtaining and furnishing such list and on such other conditions as the Court deems appropriate. Where the stockholder seeks to inspect the corporation’s books and records, other than its stock ledger or list of stockholders, such stockholder shall first establish that:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(c) (src:875)
@export If the Court orders the corporation to furnish a list of its stockholders as of a specific date, must I first pay the corporation the reasonable cost of obtaining and furnishing it (s 220(c))?
GIVEN `the Court has ordered the corporation to furnish a list of its stockholders as of a specific date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered the corporation to furnish a list of its stockholders as of a specific date?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I first pay the cost of the list of stockholders the Court orders` IF
    `s 220(c) the stockholder must first pay the corporation the reasonable cost of obtaining and furnishing the list` `the Court has ordered the corporation to furnish a list of its stockholders as of a specific date`

-- src:875 | Where the stockholder seeks to inspect the corporation’s books and records, other than its stock ledger or list of stockholders, such stockholder shall first establish that:
-- src:876 | (1) Such stockholder is a stockholder;
-- src:877 | (2) Such stockholder has complied with this section respecting the form and manner of making demand for inspection of such documents; and
-- src:878 | (3) The inspection such stockholder seeks is for a proper purpose.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(c)(1) to (3) (src:875-878)
@export For books and records other than the stock ledger and the list of stockholders, have I first established what section 220(c) requires: that I am a stockholder, that I complied with the form and manner of demand, and that the inspection is for a proper purpose?
GIVEN `I have established that I am a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you established that you are a stockholder?
      `I have established that I complied with section 220 respecting the form and manner of making demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you established that you complied with section 220 respecting the form and manner of making demand?
      `I have established that the inspection I seek is for a proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you established that the inspection you seek is for a proper purpose?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I first established what section 220(c) requires for books and records` IF
    `s 220(c) the stockholder has first established what the subsection requires for books and records other than the stock ledger and list of stockholders` `I have established that I am a stockholder` `I have established that I complied with section 220 respecting the form and manner of making demand` `I have established that the inspection I seek is for a proper purpose`

-- src:879 | Where the stockholder seeks to inspect the corporation’s stock ledger or list of stockholders and establishes that such stockholder is a stockholder and has complied with this section respecting the form and manner of making demand for inspection of such documents, the burden of proof shall be upon the corporation to establish that the inspection such stockholder seeks is for an improper purpose. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(c) (src:879)
@export Who bears the burden of proof as to the purpose of my inspection (s 220(c))? Me, for books and records; the corporation, for the stock ledger or list once I have established I am a stockholder and complied with the form and manner of demand. Returns nothing while I have not yet established those two matters for the ledger or list.
GIVEN `I seek to inspect the stock ledger or the list of stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you seek to inspect the stock ledger or the list of stockholders (rather than other books and records)?
      `I have established that I am a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you established that you are a stockholder?
      `I have established that I complied with section 220 respecting the form and manner of making demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you established that you complied with section 220 respecting the form and manner of making demand?
GIVETH A MAYBE Actor
DECIDE `Who bears the burden of proof as to the purpose of my inspection` IS
    `s 220(c) the party who bears the burden of proof as to the purpose of the inspection` `I seek to inspect the stock ledger or the list of stockholders` `I have established that I am a stockholder` `I have established that I complied with section 220 respecting the form and manner of making demand`

-- Situation: I am a director.
§§ `s 220(d) A director's right to examine`

-- src:880 | Any director shall have the right to examine the corporation’s stock ledger, a list of its stockholders, its books and records, and other corporate records for a purpose reasonably related to the director’s position as a director. The Court of Chancery is hereby vested with the exclusive jurisdiction to determine whether a director is entitled to the inspection sought. The Court may summarily order the corporation to permit the director to inspect the stock ledger, the list of stockholders, the books and records, and other corporate records and to make copies or extracts therefrom. The burden of proof shall be upon the corporation to establish that the inspection such director seeks is for an improper purpose. The Court may, in its discretion, prescribe any limitations or conditions with reference to the inspection, or award such other and further relief as the Court may deem just and proper.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(d) (src:880)
@export As a director, do I have the right to examine the corporation's stock ledger, a list of its stockholders, its books and records and other corporate records (s 220(d))?
GIVEN `I am a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director?
      `my purpose is reasonably related to my position as a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your purpose reasonably related to your position as a director?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As a director, may I examine the stock ledger, the list of stockholders and the corporation's records` IF
    `s 220(d) the director has the right to examine the stock ledger, the list of stockholders, the books and records and other corporate records` `I am a director` `my purpose is reasonably related to my position as a director`

-- src:880 | The Court of Chancery is hereby vested with the exclusive jurisdiction to determine whether a director is entitled to the inspection sought. The Court may summarily order the corporation to permit the director to inspect the stock ledger, the list of stockholders, the books and records, and other corporate records and to make copies or extracts therefrom. The burden of proof shall be upon the corporation to establish that the inspection such director seeks is for an improper purpose. The Court may, in its discretion, prescribe any limitations or conditions with reference to the inspection, or award such other and further relief as the Court may deem just and proper.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(d) (src:880)
@export May the Court of Chancery make this order on a director's application under section 220(d)?
GIVEN `the order` IS A `s 220(d) Order the Court may make on a director's application` @desc Which order: a summary order to permit the director to inspect and copy; a limitation or condition on the inspection; or such other and further relief as is just and proper?
      `the director has applied to the Court of Chancery under section 220(d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the director applied to the Court of Chancery under section 220(d)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Court of Chancery make this order on a director's application` IF
    `s 220(d) the Court of Chancery may make the order` `the order` `the director has applied to the Court of Chancery under section 220(d)`

-- src:880 | The burden of proof shall be upon the corporation to establish that the inspection such director seeks is for an improper purpose. The Court may, in its discretion, prescribe any limitations or conditions with reference to the inspection, or award such other and further relief as the Court may deem just and proper.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(d) (src:880)
@export Who bears the burden of proof that the inspection a director seeks is for an improper purpose (s 220(d))?
GIVETH A Actor
DECIDE `Who must prove that a director's inspection is for an improper purpose` IS
    `s 220(d) the party who bears the burden of proof that the inspection the director seeks is for an improper purpose`

§§ `s 220(e) to (h) Records beyond the books and records`

-- src:881 | (e) Except as otherwise expressly provided in subsection (f) or subsection (g) of this section, in any proceeding brought by a stockholder under subsection (c) of this section to compel the inspection of books and records, the Court of Chancery may not order the corporation to produce any records of the corporation other than the books and records set forth in paragraph (a)(1) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(e) (src:881)
@export May the Court of Chancery order the corporation to produce this record in a stockholder's proceeding under section 220(c) (s 220(e))?
GIVEN `the record is among the books and records set forth in section 220(a)(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the record among the books and records set forth in section 220(a)(1)?
      `the record is the stock ledger or a list of stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the stock ledger or a list of stockholders?
      `the Court may order the record produced under section 220(f)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May the Court order it produced under section 220(f)?
      `the Court may order the record produced under section 220(g)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May the Court order it produced under section 220(g)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Court of Chancery order the corporation to produce this record in a stockholder's proceeding` IF
    `s 220(e) the Court of Chancery may order the corporation to produce the record in a stockholder's proceeding` `the record is among the books and records set forth in section 220(a)(1)` `the record is the stock ledger or a list of stockholders` `the Court may order the record produced under section 220(f)` `the Court may order the record produced under section 220(g)`

-- src:882 | (f) If the corporation does not have any of the books and records described in paragraph (a)(1)c., (a)(1)e., or (a)(1)g. of this section or, in the case of a corporation that has a class of stock listed on a national securities exchange, paragraph (a)(1)i. of this section, the Court of Chancery may order the corporation to produce additional records of the corporation constituting the functional equivalent of any such books and records in response to a demand for inspection brought by a stockholder under subsection (b) of this section only if and to the extent the stockholder has met the requirements of subsection (b) of this section, and only to the extent necessary and essential to fulfill the stockholder’s proper purpose.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(f) (src:882)
@export May the Court of Chancery order the corporation to produce additional records constituting the functional equivalent of books and records it does not have (s 220(f))?
GIVEN `the corporation does not have any of the books and records described in paragraphs (a)(1)c., e. or g.` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation not have any of the books and records described in section 220(a)(1)c. (minutes of stockholder meetings and consents), e. (board and committee minutes and records) or g. (annual financial statements)?
      `the corporation has a class of stock listed on a national securities exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation have a class of stock listed on a national securities exchange?
      `the corporation does not have the books and records described in paragraph (a)(1)i.` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation not have director and officer independence questionnaires (section 220(a)(1)i.)?
      `the stockholder has met the requirements of section 220(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the stockholder met the requirements of section 220(b)?
      `the records are the functional equivalent of the books and records the corporation does not have` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the records sought the functional equivalent of the books and records the corporation does not have?
      `the records are necessary and essential to fulfill the stockholder's proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they necessary and essential to fulfill the stockholder's proper purpose?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Court of Chancery order the functional equivalent of records the corporation does not have` IF
    `s 220(f) the Court of Chancery may order the corporation to produce the additional records constituting the functional equivalent` `the corporation does not have any of the books and records described in paragraphs (a)(1)c., e. or g.` `the corporation has a class of stock listed on a national securities exchange` `the corporation does not have the books and records described in paragraph (a)(1)i.` `the stockholder has met the requirements of section 220(b)` `the records are the functional equivalent of the books and records the corporation does not have` `the records are necessary and essential to fulfill the stockholder's proper purpose`

-- src:883 | (g) In any proceeding brought by a stockholder under subsection (c) of this section to compel the inspection of books and records, the Court of Chancery may order the corporation to produce, in addition to any books and records or other records ordered to be produced under subsection (e) of this section, other specific records of the corporation only if and to the extent:
-- src:884 | (1) Such stockholder has met the requirements of subsection (b) of this section;
-- src:885 | (2) Such stockholder has made a showing of a compelling need for an inspection of such records to further the stockholder’s proper purpose; and
-- src:886 | (3) Such stockholder has demonstrated by clear and convincing evidence that such specific records are necessary and essential to further such purpose.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(g) (src:883-886)
@export May the Court of Chancery order the corporation to produce other specific records (s 220(g))?
GIVEN `the stockholder has met the requirements of section 220(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the stockholder met the requirements of section 220(b)?
      `the stockholder has made a showing of a compelling need for an inspection of the records to further the proper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the stockholder made a showing of a compelling need for an inspection of the records to further the stockholder's proper purpose?
      `the stockholder has demonstrated by clear and convincing evidence that the specific records are necessary and essential to further that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the stockholder demonstrated by clear and convincing evidence that the specific records are necessary and essential to further that purpose?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Court of Chancery order the corporation to produce other specific records` IF
    `s 220(g) the Court of Chancery may order the corporation to produce the other specific records` `the stockholder has met the requirements of section 220(b)` `the stockholder has made a showing of a compelling need for an inspection of the records to further the proper purpose` `the stockholder has demonstrated by clear and convincing evidence that the specific records are necessary and essential to further that purpose`

-- src:887 | (h) The Court of Chancery may impose reasonable restrictions as provided in paragraph (b)(3) of this section to any records of the corporation produced under subsection (f) or subsection (g) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 220(h) (src:887)
@export May the Court of Chancery impose reasonable restrictions, as in section 220(b)(3), on records produced under section 220(f) or (g) (s 220(h))? Returns nothing for records produced otherwise.
GIVEN `the records are produced under section 220(f) or (g)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the records produced under section 220(f) or section 220(g)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Court of Chancery impose restrictions on records produced under section 220(f) or (g)` IS
    `s 220(h) the Court of Chancery may impose reasonable restrictions as provided in paragraph (b)(3) on the records` `the records are produced under section 220(f) or (g)`
